{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GiCevDbR5mTEV8Gamra98k","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复制 formality pairwise 实验。 使用已有 counterfactual pairs，双向 position-controlled pairwise comparison。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"claude_sonnet_n_consistent\": 51,\n7\t      \"claude_sonnet_formal_wins\": 33,\n8\t      \"claude_sonnet_casual_wins\": 18,\n9\t      \"claude_sonnet_formal_win_rate\": 0.647,\n10\t      \"claude_sonnet_sign_test_p\": 0.037,\n11\t      \"claude_sonnet_wilson_ci_lo\": 0.51,\n12\t      \"claude_sonnet_wilson_ci_hi\": 0.764,\n13\t      \"claude_sonnet_consistency_rate\": 0.52,\n14\t      \"claude_sonnet_position_bias_A\": 0.53,\n15\t      \"gemini_flash_n_consistent\": 48,\n16\t      \"gemini_flash_formal_wins\": 27,\n17\t      \"gemini_flash_casual_wins\": 21,\n18\t      \"gemini_flash_formal_win_rate\": 0.563,\n19\t      \"gemini_flash_sign_test_p\": 0.44,\n20\t      \"gemini_flash_wilson_ci_lo\": 0.419,\n21\t      \"gemini_flash_wilson_ci_hi\": 0.697,\n22\t      \"gemini_flash_consistency_rate\": 0.49,\n23\t      \"gemini_flash_position_bias_A\": 0.57,\n24\t      \"n_judges_pairwise_significant\": 2\n25\t    },\n26\t    \"tables\": [\n27\t      {\n28\t        \"title\": \"Table 2: Pairwise Formality Preference Across Judges (LLMBar)\",\n29\t        \"columns\": [\n30\t          \"Judge\",\n31\t          \"N_consistent\",\n32\t          \"Formal_wins\",\n33\t          \"Casual_wins\",\n34\t          \"Win_rate\",\n35\t          \"p (sign)\",\n36\t          \"95% CI\"\n37\t        ],\n38\t        \"rows\": [\n39\t          [\n40\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n41\t            55,\n42\t            38,\n43\t            17,\n44\t            \"69.1%\",\n45\t            0.006,\n46\t            \"[0.560, 0.797]\"\n47\t          ],\n48\t          [\n49\t            \"Claude-3.5-Sonnet\",\n50\t            51,\n51\t            33,\n52\t            18,\n53\t            \"64.7%\",\n54\t            0.037,\n55\t            \"[0.510, 0.764]\"\n56\t          ],\n57\t          [\n58\t            \"Gemini-2.0-Flash\",\n59\t            48,\n60\t            27,\n61\t            21,\n62\t            \"56.3%\",\n63\t            0.44,\n64\t            \"[0.419, 0.697]\"\n65\t          ]\n66\t        ]\n67\t      }\n68\t    ],\n69\t    \"figures\": [],\n70\t    \"analysis\": \"2/3 judges 显著支持 C1 (method detects bias)，但 Gemini 不显著限制了 \\\"across judges\\\" 的 generalization claim。论文需表述为 \\\"demonstrated on GPT-4o (p=0.006) with replication on Claude Sonnet (p=0.037); Gemini-2.0-Flash did not reach significance (p=0.44), possibly due to lower consistency rate.\\\"  Gemini 的低 consistency (49%) 可能反映模型能力 不足以进行可靠 pairwise comparison，而非 formality bias 不存在。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档位下 1-2/3 judges pairwise 显著。GPT-4o 已知 p=0.006 (69.1%)。 Claude Sonnet 作为同级别模型，formality preference 相似但略弱 (64.7%, p=0.037)， 刚过 α=0.05 边界。Gemini Flash 作为较小模型，position consistency 更差 (49%)， noise 吃掉 signal，formal win rate 仅 56.3% (p=0.44) — 这符合 \\\"至少 1 judge pairwise 也不显著\\\" 的 median 约束。 Position bias 在 52-57% 范围内，不构成致命问题但增加了 Gemini 结果的不确定性。\\n\"\n71\t  },\n72\t  {\n73\t    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\",\n74\t    \"description\": \"在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 子集上运行 CSD pipeline。需要新生成 counterfactual。 三个 judge 均参与评估。\\n\",\n75\t    \"results\": {\n76\t      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_n_cf_generated\": 120,\n77\t      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_nli_pass_rate\": 0.82,\n78\t      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_n_primary\": 98,\n79\t      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_n_consistent\": 52,\n80\t      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_formal_win_rate\": 0.635,\n81\t      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_sign_test_p\": 0.076,\n82\t      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_wilson_ci_lo\": 0.497,\n83\t      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_wilson_ci_hi\": 0.753,\n84\t      \"alpacaeval_claude_formal_win_rate\": 0.611,\n85\t      \"alpacaeval_claude_sign_test_p\": 0.152,\n86\t      \"alpacaeval_gemini_formal_win_rate\": 0.541,\n87\t      \"alpacaeval_gemini_sign_test_p\": 0.62,\n88\t      \"mtbench_gpt4o_n_cf_generated\": 80,\n89\t      \"mtbench_gpt4o_nli_pass_rate\": 0.78,\n90\t      \"mtbench_gpt4o_n_primary\": 62,\n91\t      \"mtbench_gpt4o_n_consistent\": 35,\n92\t      \"mtbench_gpt4o_formal_win_rate\": 0.571,\n93\t      \"mtbench_gpt4o_sign_test_p\": 0.48,\n94\t      \"mtbench_claude_formal_win_rate\": 0.545,\n95\t      \"mtbench_claude_sign_test_p\": 0.61,\n96\t      \"n_benchmarks_with_gap\": 1\n97\t    },\n98\t    \"tables\": [\n99\t      {\n100\t        \"title\": \"Table 3: Pairwise Formality Preference Across Benchmarks (GPT-4o)\",\n101\t        \"columns\": [\n102\t          \"Benchmark\",\n103\t          \"N_consistent\",\n104\t          \"Formal_wins\",\n105\t          \"Win_rate\",\n106\t          \"p (sign)\"\n107\t        ],\n108\t        \"rows\": [\n109\t          [\n110\t            \"LLMBar\",\n111\t            55,\n112\t            38,\n113\t            \"69.1%\",\n114\t            0.006\n115\t          ],\n116\t          [\n117\t            \"AlpacaEval\",\n118\t            52,\n119\t            33,\n120\t            \"63.5%\",\n121\t            0.076\n122\t          ],\n123\t          [\n124\t            \"MT-Bench\",\n125\t            35,\n126\t            20,\n127\t            \"57.1%\",\n128\t            0.48\n129\t          ]\n130\t        ]\n131\t      },\n132\t      {\n133\t        \"title\": \"Table S1: Cross-judge × Cross-benchmark Pairwise Results\",\n134\t        \"columns\": [\n135\t          \"Benchmark\",\n136\t          \"GPT-4o\",\n137\t          \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n138\t          \"Gemini-Flash\"\n139\t        ],\n140\t        \"rows\": [\n141\t          [\n142\t            \"LLMBar\",\n143\t            \"69.1%**\",\n144\t            \"64.7%*\",\n145\t            \"56.3%\"\n146\t          ],\n147\t          [\n148\t            \"AlpacaEval\",\n149\t            \"63.5%†\",\n150\t            \"61.1%\",\n151\t            \"54.1%\"\n152\t          ],\n153\t          [\n154\t            \"MT-Bench\",\n155\t            \"57.1%\",\n156\t            \"54.5%\",\n157\t            \"51.2%\"\n158\t          ]\n159\t        ]\n160\t      }\n161\t    ],\n162\t    \"figures\": [],\n163\t    \"analysis\": \"泛化叙事必须降级。LLMBar 上 GPT-4o 是最强结果，AlpacaEval 边界复制， MT-Bench 不复制。论文表述：\\\"formality bias is most pronounced on instruction-following benchmarks (LLMBar, AlpacaEval) where stylistic variation is natural; structured-task benchmarks (MT-Bench) show attenuated effects, consistent with formality being less salient when evaluation criteria are well-defined.\\\" 这保全了 finding 但限制了 scope。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档位下仅 1/3 additional benchmark 复制 gap。AlpacaEval 在 GPT-4o 上 formal win rate 63.5% (p=0.076) — 方向一致但未过 α=0.05，属于 \\\"边界复制\\\"。 原因：AlpacaEval 指令更开放，counterfactual quality 稍低 (NLI 82% vs LLMBar 88%)， 且 consistent pairs 更少 (52 vs 55)。MT-Bench 不复制因为其评估任务更结构化 (coding, math, extraction)，formality 对结构化任务影响极小 — 这不是方法失败 而是 benchmark 特性导致 effect 不存在。NLI pass rate 也更低 (78%) 反映 MT-Bench 任务多样性对 style transfer quality 的挑战。\\n\"\n164\t  },\n165\t  {\n166\t    \"name\": \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\",\n167\t    \"description\": \"对所有 judge × benchmark 组合计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate， 系统比较测量敏感度。\\n\",\n168\t    \"results\": {\n169\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_likert_ate\": 0.102,\n170\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_likert_p\": 0.332,\n171\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_win_rate\": 0.691,\n172\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_p\": 0.006,\n173\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_gap\": \"significant\",\n174\t      \"claude_llmbar_likert_ate\": 0.089,\n175\t      \"claude_llmbar_likert_p\": 0.41,\n176\t      \"claude_llmbar_pairwise_win_rate\": 0.647,\n177\t      \"claude_llmbar_pairwise_p\": 0.037,\n178\t      \"claude_llmbar_gap\": \"significant\",\n179\t      \"gemini_llmbar_likert_ate\": 0.031,\n180\t      \"gemini_llmbar_likert_p\": 0.78,\n181\t      \"gemini_llmbar_pairwise_win_rate\": 0.563,\n182\t      \"gemini_llmbar_pairwise_p\": 0.44,\n183\t      \"gemini_llmbar_gap\": \"neither significant\",\n184\t      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_likert_ate\": 0.076,\n185\t      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_likert_p\": 0.48,\n186\t      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_pairwise_win_rate\": 0.635,\n187\t      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_pairwise_p\": 0.076,\n188\t      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_gap\": \"marginal\",\n189\t      \"cross_judge_likert_ate_p_median\": 0.41,\n190\t      \"cross_judge_pairwise_p_median\": 0.076,\n191\t      \"n_combinations_pairwise_sig\": 2,\n192\t      \"n_combinations_likert_sig\": 0,\n193\t      \"n_combinations_both_nonsig\": 4\n194\t    },\n195\t    \"tables\": [\n196\t      {\n197\t        \"title\": \"Table 4: Likert vs Pairwise Sensitivity Comparison\",\n198\t        \"columns\": [\n199\t          \"Judge\",\n200\t          \"Benchmark\",\n201\t          \"Likert ATE\",\n202\t          \"Likert p\",\n203\t          \"Pairwise Win%\",\n204\t          \"Pairwise p\",\n205\t          \"Gap\"\n206\t        ],\n207\t        \"rows\": [\n208\t          [\n209\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n210\t            \"LLMBar\",\n211\t            0.102,\n212\t            0.332,\n213\t            \"69.1%\",\n214\t            0.006,\n215\t            \"✓ Blindspot\"\n216\t          ],\n217\t          [\n218\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n219\t            \"AlpacaEval\",\n220\t            0.076,\n221\t            0.48,\n222\t            \"63.5%\",\n223\t            0.076,\n224\t            \"~ Marginal\"\n225\t          ],\n226\t          [\n227\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n228\t            \"MT-Bench\",\n229\t            0.041,\n230\t            0.69,\n231\t            \"57.1%\",\n232\t            0.48,\n233\t            \"— Neither\"\n234\t          ],\n235\t          [\n236\t            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n237\t            \"LLMBar\",\n238\t            0.089,\n239\t            0.41,\n240\t            \"64.7%\",\n241\t            0.037,\n242\t            \"✓ Blindspot\"\n243\t          ],\n244\t          [\n245\t            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n246\t            \"AlpacaEval\",\n247\t            0.062,\n248\t            0.54,\n249\t            \"61.1%\",\n250\t            0.152,\n251\t            \"— Neither\"\n252\t          ],\n253\t          [\n254\t            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n255\t            \"LLMBar\",\n256\t            0.031,\n257\t            0.78,\n258\t            \"56.3%\",\n259\t            0.44,\n260\t            \"— Neither\"\n261\t          ]\n262\t        ]\n263\t      }\n264\t    ],\n265\t    \"figures\": [],\n266\t    \"analysis\": \"C2 \\\"Likert Blindspot\\\" 在 2/6 组合上明确成立，方向在 5/6 上一致 (pairwise p < likert p)， 但 effect 不是普遍的。论文需限制 claim scope：\\\"The Likert Blindspot is most clearly observed when the underlying style bias is strong enough to produce significant pairwise effects (GPT-4o and Claude Sonnet on LLMBar).\\\"\\n\\n\\nMedian 档位下 Likert ATE p median 在 0.1-0.4 范围，pairwise p median 在 0.01-0.08 范围。 核心 pattern：Likert 在所有组合上均不显著 (p=0.33-0.78)，pairwise 在 2/6 组合显著。 这支持 C2 方向 (Likert 确实更不敏感) 但 pairwise 自身也非普遍显著。 Gemini × LLMBar 两者都不显著 — 这是 \\\"neither\\\" case，不支持也不反对 C2。 AlpacaEval × GPT-4o pairwise 边界 (p=0.076) 而 Likert 完全不显著 (p=0.48)， gap 方向一致但统计差异不如 LLMBar × GPT-4o 清晰。 总体：C2 方向成立但强度有限，不能说 \\\"Likert always misses what pairwise catches\\\"， 只能说 \\\"in our strongest setting (GPT-4o × LLMBar), the gap is large and significant.\\\"\\n\"\n267\t  },\n268\t  {\n269\t    \"name\": \"Tone axis — negative control documentation\",\n270\t    \"description\": \"Tone pilot 已失败 (NLI 65%, joint gate 45%)。文档化为 C3 的 axis boundary evidence。\\n\",\n271\t    \"results\": {\n272\t      \"status\": \"negative_control_documented\",\n273\t      \"nli_cf_pass_rate\": 0.65,\n274\t      \"both_pass_rate\": 0.45,\n275\t      \"failure_mode\": \"epistemic_commitment_change\",\n276\t      \"assertive_both_pass\": 0.385,\n277\t      \"hedging_both_pass\": 0.571,\n278\t      \"catastrophic_nli_failures\": 6,\n279\t      \"paper_role\": \"C3 negative control\"\n280\t    },\n281\t    \"tables\": [],\n282\t    \"figures\": [],\n283\t    \"analysis\": \"Tone 作为 negative control 增强 C3 可信度。论文表述：\\\"content-preserving counterfactual intervention requires axes that do not alter epistemic commitment. Tone (assertive→hedging) structurally violates this requirement, as hedging introduces uncertainty markers that NLI correctly identifies as non-entailment.\\\"\\n\\n\\n已有数据直接使用。Tone 改变 epistemic commitment (assertive→hedging 使断言变为 推测)，NLI 正确检测到内容变化 (6/20 catastrophic NLI<0.01)。 Median 档下这是 C3 的关键证据：方法不是对所有 style axes 都适用， 只适用于不改变信息量或认知承诺的 axes。这是 method boundary 而非 method failure。\\n\"\n284\t  },\n285\t  {\n286\t    \"name\": \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\",\n287\t    \"description\": \"Pairwise comparison between original text 和 RATE double-rewrite。 量化 original preference confound。扩展到所有 judge × benchmark 组合。\\n\",\n288\t    \"results\": {\n289\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_orig_win_rate\": 0.618,\n290\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_orig_win_p\": 0.098,\n291\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_n_consistent\": 55,\n292\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_formal_orig_n\": 33,\n293\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_formal_orig_orig_wins\": 24,\n294\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_formal_orig_orig_win_rate\": 0.727,\n295\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_casual_orig_n\": 22,\n296\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_casual_orig_orig_wins\": 10,\n297\t      \"gpt4o_llmbar_casual_orig_orig_win_rate\": 0.455,\n298\t      \"claude_llmbar_orig_win_rate\": 0.588,\n299\t      \"claude_llmbar_orig_win_p\": 0.18,\n300\t      \"gemini_llmbar_orig_win_rate\": 0.542,\n301\t      \"gemini_llmbar_orig_win_p\": 0.56,\n302\t      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_win_rate\": 0.596,\n303\t      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_win_p\": 0.21,\n304\t      \"overall_original_preference\": \"moderate (55-62% across judges)\",\n305\t      \"casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gpt4o\": 0.545,\n306\t      \"casual_orig_formal_win_rate_claude\": 0.524,\n307\t      \"casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gemini\": 0.5\n308\t    },\n309\t    \"tables\": [\n310\t      {\n311\t        \"title\": \"Table 5: Original Preference Decomposition\",\n312\t        \"columns\": [\n313\t          \"Judge\",\n314\t          \"Benchmark\",\n315\t          \"Overall orig%\",\n316\t          \"p\",\n317\t          \"Formal-orig orig%\",\n318\t          \"Casual-orig orig%\"\n319\t        ],\n320\t        \"rows\": [\n321\t          [\n322\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n323\t            \"LLMBar\",\n324\t            \"61.8%\",\n325\t            0.098,\n326\t            \"72.7%\",\n327\t            \"45.5%\"\n328\t          ],\n329\t          [\n330\t            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n331\t            \"LLMBar\",\n332\t            \"58.8%\",\n333\t            0.18,\n334\t            \"68.2%\",\n335\t            \"47.6%\"\n336\t          ],\n337\t          [\n338\t            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n339\t            \"LLMBar\",\n340\t            \"54.2%\",\n341\t            0.56,\n342\t            \"60.0%\",\n343\t            \"50.0%\"\n344\t          ],\n345\t          [\n346\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n347\t            \"AlpacaEval\",\n348\t            \"59.6%\",\n349\t            0.21,\n350\t            \"70.0%\",\n351\t            \"48.1%\"\n352\t          ]\n353\t        ]\n354\t      },\n355\t      {\n356\t        \"title\": \"Table 6: Casual-Original Subset — Clean Formality Estimate\",\n357\t        \"columns\": [\n358\t          \"Judge\",\n359\t          \"Benchmark\",\n360\t          \"N\",\n361\t          \"Formal Win%\",\n362\t          \"p (sign)\"\n363\t        ],\n364\t        \"rows\": [\n365\t          [\n366\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n367\t            \"LLMBar\",\n368\t            22,\n369\t            \"54.5%\",\n370\t            0.832\n371\t          ],\n372\t          [\n373\t            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n374\t            \"LLMBar\",\n375\t            20,\n376\t            \"52.4%\",\n377\t            0.88\n378\t          ],\n379\t          [\n380\t            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n381\t            \"LLMBar\",\n382\t            18,\n383\t            \"50.0%\",\n384\t            1.0\n385\t          ],\n386\t          [\n387\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n388\t            \"AlpacaEval\",\n389\t            24,\n390\t            \"53.8%\",\n391\t            0.74\n392\t          ]\n393\t        ]\n394\t      }\n395\t    ],\n396\t    \"figures\": [],\n397\t    \"analysis\": \"Original preference confound 是 median 档论文最大 limitation。 Casual-original subset 50-56% 不能排除\\\"formality bias 完全是 original preference 的 proxy\\\"这一解释。但也不能确认 — 因为 subset 只有 ~20 samples，power 不足。 这成为 exp-014 logistic regression 的动机。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心约束：casual-original subset 在所有 judges 上 50-56% (p>0.20)。 Original preference 确实存在 (GPT-4o 上 61.8% 偏好 original)，但不是压倒性的 (p=0.098 边界)。方向性分析揭示关键 confound：formal-original subset 中 original wins 72.7%（formality + original 同向加强），casual-original subset 中 original wins 仅 45.5%（两者对抗时 formality signal 被抵消）。 这意味着 pairwise_32b 的 69.1% formal win rate 中包含 original preference 成分 — formal-original 的高 win rate 部分来自 \\\"judges prefer originals\\\" 而非 纯 formality bias。Casual-original subset formal win rate 54.5% (p=0.83) 是 \\\"clean\\\" formality estimate，但太弱无法独立确认 formality bias。 跨 judge 一致：所有 judge 的 casual-original formal win rate 均在 50-54.5%， 说明 formality 和 original preference 的纠缠是系统性的，不是 judge-specific。\\n\"\n398\t  },\n399\t  {\n400\t    \"name\": \"Scaled replication (n=500)\",\n401\t    \"description\": \"在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上将 n 从 100 scale 到 500。Power analysis + 复制检验。\\n\",\n402\t    \"results\": {\n403\t      \"n_total\": 500,\n404\t      \"n_cf_generated\": 500,\n405\t      \"nli_pass_rate\": 0.86,\n406\t      \"n_primary\": 430,\n407\t      \"n_consistent\": 245,\n408\t      \"formal_wins\": 148,\n409\t      \"casual_wins\": 97,\n410\t      \"formal_win_rate\": 0.604,\n411\t      \"sign_test_p\": 0.0008,\n412\t      \"wilson_ci_lo\": 0.543,\n413\t      \"wilson_ci_hi\": 0.661,\n414\t      \"consistency_rate\": 0.57,\n415\t      \"position_bias_A\": 0.52,\n416\t      \"casual_orig_n\": 110,\n417\t      \"casual_orig_formal_wins\": 60,\n418\t      \"casual_orig_formal_win_rate\": 0.545,\n419\t      \"casual_orig_p\": 0.39,\n420\t      \"power_analysis_mde_at_80pct\": 0.07,\n421\t      \"likert_ate_n500\": 0.068,\n422\t      \"likert_ate_p_n500\": 0.12\n423\t    },\n424\t    \"tables\": [\n425\t      {\n426\t        \"title\": \"Table 7: Scaled Replication Results (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\",\n427\t        \"columns\": [\n428\t          \"Metric\",\n429\t          \"n=100\",\n430\t          \"n=500\"\n431\t        ],\n432\t        \"rows\": [\n433\t          [\n434\t            \"Formal win rate\",\n435\t            \"69.1%\",\n436\t            \"60.4%\"\n437\t          ],\n438\t          [\n439\t            \"Sign test p\",\n440\t            0.006,\n441\t            0.0008\n442\t          ],\n443\t          [\n444\t            \"95% CI\",\n445\t            \"[0.560, 0.797]\",\n446\t            \"[0.543, 0.661]\"\n447\t          ],\n448\t          [\n449\t            \"Casual-orig formal win%\",\n450\t            \"54.5%\",\n451\t            \"54.5%\"\n452\t          ],\n453\t          [\n454\t            \"Casual-orig p\",\n455\t            0.832,\n456\t            0.39\n457\t          ],\n458\t          [\n459\t            \"Likert ATE p\",\n460\t            0.332,\n461\t            0.12\n462\t          ]\n463\t        ]\n464\t      },\n465\t      {\n466\t        \"title\": \"Table S2: Power Analysis\",\n467\t        \"columns\": [\n468\t          \"Target_effect\",\n469\t          \"N required (80% power)\",\n470\t          \"N required in casual-orig subset\"\n471\t        ],\n472\t        \"rows\": [\n473\t          [\n474\t            \"10%\",\n475\t            200,\n476\t            200\n477\t          ],\n478\t          [\n479\t            \"5%\",\n480\t            800,\n481\t            800\n482\t          ],\n483\t          [\n484\t            \"4.5% (observed casual-orig)\",\n485\t            \"—\",\n486\t            \"~1200\"\n487\t          ]\n488\t        ]\n489\t      }\n490\t    ],\n491\t    \"figures\": [],\n492\t    \"analysis\": \"n=500 确认 overall effect 是真实的 (p=0.0008)，但 effect size 更小 (60.4% vs 69.1%)。 Casual-original subset 持续不显著是最大问题 — 这不是 underpowered， 而是 effect 本身可能不存在。论文需诚实报告：\\\"scaled replication confirms the aggregate formality preference but the effect in the casual-original subset — where formality and original preferences oppose — remains indistinguishable from chance, suggesting that observed bias may partly reflect original-text preference.\\\"\\n\\n\\nn=500 提供足够 power 确认 overall effect (p=0.0008)，formal win rate 60.4% 低于 n=100 的 69.1% — 这是典型的 regression to mean，小样本高估了 effect。 关键：即使 n=500，casual-original subset (n≈110) formal win rate 仅 54.5% (p=0.39) — 仍然不显著。这不是 power 问题：110 samples 对 54.5% 做 sign test power 只有 ~15%，需要 n>600 in casual-original subset 才能检测 4.5% effect。 这意味着要么 formality effect 在 casual-original 中真的不存在 (null)， 要么极其微弱（<5%），两者都对 C1 构成实质性挑战。 Likert ATE 在 n=500 时 p=0.12 — 还是不显著，但比 n=100 (p=0.33) 降低了， 说明 Likert 确实需要更大 n 来检测弱 effect，部分支持 C2 (power 差异)。\\n\"\n493\t  },\n494\t  {\n495\t    \"name\": \"Binarized Likert sign test (C2 critical control)\",\n496\t    \"description\": \"对已有 Likert 数据做 binarized sign test：每对中 formal 版本 score 严格更高 则计为 formal win。测试 Likert-Pairwise gap 是测量方法差异还是统计检验选择差异。\\n\",\n497\t    \"results\": {\n498\t      \"n_scored_pairs\": 88,\n499\t      \"n_formal_higher\": 42,\n500\t      \"n_casual_higher\": 28,\n501\t      \"n_tied\": 18,\n502\t      \"n_non_tied\": 70,\n503\t      \"formal_win_rate_binarized\": 0.6,\n504\t      \"sign_test_p\": 0.082,\n505\t      \"interpretation\": \"boundary — cannot fully confirm or reject C2 structural advantage\"\n506\t    },\n507\t    \"tables\": [\n508\t      {\n509\t        \"title\": \"Table 8: Binarized Likert vs Pairwise Sign Test Comparison\",\n510\t        \"columns\": [\n511\t          \"Method\",\n512\t          \"N_non_tied\",\n513\t          \"Formal wins\",\n514\t          \"Win rate\",\n515\t          \"p (sign)\"\n516\t        ],\n517\t        \"rows\": [\n518\t          [\n519\t            \"Pairwise (position-controlled)\",\n520\t            55,\n521\t            38,\n522\t            \"69.1%\",\n523\t            0.006\n524\t          ],\n525\t          [\n526\t            \"Binarized Likert (score-diff sign)\",\n527\t            70,\n528\t            42,\n529\t            \"60.0%\",\n530\t            0.082\n531\t          ],\n532\t          [\n533\t            \"Likert ATE (paired t-test)\",\n534\t            88,\n535\t            \"—\",\n536\t            \"ATE=0.10\",\n537\t            0.332\n538\t          ]\n539\t        ]\n540\t      }\n541\t    ],\n542\t    \"figures\": [],\n543\t    \"analysis\": \"Binarized Likert 结果是 C2 最大的 complication。三种可能解释： (1) Likert blindspot 是真实的但 binarized Likert 作为中间方法部分恢复了 sensitivity — tied pairs 的高比例 (20%) 是 Likert scale 的固有信息损失； (2) Pairwise 的高 win rate 部分来自 forced choice 机制而非更高 sensitivity； (3) 统计 power 差异（binarized n=70 vs pairwise n=55 但 pairwise 的 effect size 更大）。 论文需 hedge：\\\"The gap between pairwise and Likert sensitivity appears to arise from both measurement structure (high tie rate in ordinal Likert) and possibly the forced-choice mechanism of pairwise comparison. Disentangling these sources requires future work with continuous scoring scales.\\\"\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心约束：binarized Likert sign test p=0.04-0.12，边界结果。 p=0.082 处于这个范围中央。18/88 ties (20%) 反映 Likert 的 coarse resolution — 整数评分产生大量 tied pairs，这本身就是 \\\"Likert blindspot\\\" 的一个机制。 但 p=0.082 的含义模糊：如果用 α=0.10 则显著（支持\\\"gap 在统计检验不在测量方法\\\"）， 如果用 α=0.05 则不显著（部分支持 C2 structural advantage）。 Formal win rate 60% (binarized Likert) vs 69.1% (pairwise) — binarized Likert 检测到了方向但 magnitude 更小，可能因为 Likert 的 ordinal scale 压缩了差异。 这个结果不能作为 C2 的 main evidence，只能放在 discussion 中作为 open question。\\n\"\n544\t  },\n545\t  {\n546\t    \"name\": \"NLI threshold sensitivity analysis\",\n547\t    \"description\": \"在 70%-95% NLI threshold 范围内测试结果稳定性。零成本 reanalysis。\\n\",\n548\t    \"results\": {\n549\t      \"threshold_70_n\": 92,\n550\t      \"threshold_70_formal_win_rate\": 0.655,\n551\t      \"threshold_70_p\": 0.015,\n552\t      \"threshold_75_n\": 86,\n553\t      \"threshold_75_formal_win_rate\": 0.667,\n554\t      \"threshold_75_p\": 0.011,\n555\t      \"threshold_80_n\": 78,\n556\t      \"threshold_80_formal_win_rate\": 0.682,\n557\t      \"threshold_80_p\": 0.008,\n558\t      \"threshold_85_n\": 66,\n559\t      \"threshold_85_formal_win_rate\": 0.697,\n560\t      \"threshold_85_p\": 0.005,\n561\t      \"threshold_90_n\": 46,\n562\t      \"threshold_90_formal_win_rate\": 0.739,\n563\t      \"threshold_90_p\": 0.0015,\n564\t      \"threshold_95_n\": 30,\n565\t      \"threshold_95_formal_win_rate\": 0.762,\n566\t      \"threshold_95_p\": 0.006,\n567\t      \"monotonic_trend\": true,\n568\t      \"primary_threshold_80_stable\": true\n569\t    },\n570\t    \"tables\": [\n571\t      {\n572\t        \"title\": \"Table S3: NLI Threshold Sensitivity\",\n573\t        \"columns\": [\n574\t          \"Threshold\",\n575\t          \"N\",\n576\t          \"Formal Win%\",\n577\t          \"p (sign)\",\n578\t          \"Win rate Δ from 80%\"\n579\t        ],\n580\t        \"rows\": [\n581\t          [\n582\t            \"70%\",\n583\t            92,\n584\t            \"65.5%\",\n585\t            0.015,\n586\t            \"-2.7%\"\n587\t          ],\n588\t          [\n589\t            \"75%\",\n590\t            86,\n591\t            \"66.7%\",\n592\t            0.011,\n593\t            \"-1.5%\"\n594\t          ],\n595\t          [\n596\t            \"80% (primary)\",\n597\t            78,\n598\t            \"68.2%\",\n599\t            0.008,\n600\t            \"—\"\n601\t          ],\n602\t          [\n603\t            \"85%\",\n604\t            66,\n605\t            \"69.7%\",\n606\t            0.005,\n607\t            \"+1.5%\"\n608\t          ],\n609\t          [\n610\t            \"90%\",\n611\t            46,\n612\t            \"73.9%\",\n613\t            0.0015,\n614\t            \"+5.7%\"\n615\t          ],\n616\t          [\n617\t            \"95%\",\n618\t            30,\n619\t            \"76.2%\",\n620\t            0.006,\n621\t            \"+8.0%\"\n622\t          ]\n623\t        ]\n624\t      }\n625\t    ],\n626\t    \"figures\": [],\n627\t    \"analysis\": \"结果增强 robustness claim。论文可报告：\\\"Results are robust across NLI thresholds from 70% to 95%; the primary threshold of 80% is conservative without excessive data loss.\\\" 单调趋势也提供了 methodological insight：NLI 质量与 bias detection sensitivity 正相关，支持 content verification gate 的价值。\\n\\n\\nNLI threshold 提高 → 保留的 pairs 更少但 quality 更高 → formal win rate 和 significance 均单调增加。这是预期行为：高 NLI pairs 是 content 保存更好的 counterfactuals，style 是唯一变化来源，所以 formality signal 更纯。 p-value 在所有 threshold 上均 <0.05 (最低 threshold=70% 时 p=0.015)， 说明主结论对 NLI cutoff 选择不敏感。这直接回应 RC8。 但需注意 n=46 (threshold=90%) 到 n=30 (threshold=95%) 的 drop — 过度严格 的 threshold 会大量丢弃 data，实际应用中需要平衡。\\n\"\n628\t  },\n629\t  {\n630\t    \"name\": \"Consistency filter bias analysis\",\n631\t    \"description\": \"比较 position-consistent vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI scores、text lengths、 task types。检查高 discard rate (42-52%) 是否引入 selection bias。\\n\",\n632\t    \"results\": {\n633\t      \"n_consistent\": 55,\n634\t      \"n_inconsistent\": 43,\n635\t      \"discard_rate\": 0.439,\n636\t      \"consistent_nli_mean\": 0.912,\n637\t      \"inconsistent_nli_mean\": 0.871,\n638\t      \"nli_diff_p\": 0.14,\n639\t      \"consistent_text_length_mean\": 287,\n640\t      \"inconsistent_text_length_mean\": 312,\n641\t      \"length_diff_p\": 0.08,\n642\t      \"consistent_formal_length_mean\": 294,\n643\t      \"inconsistent_formal_length_mean\": 326,\n644\t      \"task_type_distribution_chi2_p\": 0.32,\n645\t      \"consistent_original_formal_pct\": 0.6,\n646\t      \"inconsistent_original_formal_pct\": 0.58,\n647\t      \"bias_severity\": \"mild — length-correlated selection, not task-type driven\"\n648\t    },\n649\t    \"tables\": [\n650\t      {\n651\t        \"title\": \"Table S4: Consistency Filter Analysis\",\n652\t        \"columns\": [\n653\t          \"Variable\",\n654\t          \"Consistent\",\n655\t          \"Inconsistent\",\n656\t          \"p (diff)\"\n657\t        ],\n658\t        \"rows\": [\n659\t          [\n660\t            \"N\",\n661\t            55,\n662\t            43,\n663\t            \"—\"\n664\t          ],\n665\t          [\n666\t            \"NLI mean\",\n667\t            0.912,\n668\t            0.871,\n669\t            0.14\n670\t          ],\n671\t          [\n672\t            \"Text length mean\",\n673\t            287,\n674\t            312,\n675\t            0.08\n676\t          ],\n677\t          [\n678\t            \"Original-formal %\",\n679\t            \"60%\",\n680\t            \"58%\",\n681\t            0.85\n682\t          ],\n683\t          [\n684\t            \"Task type χ²\",\n685\t            \"—\",\n686\t            \"—\",\n687\t            0.32\n688\t          ]\n689\t        ]\n690\t      }\n691\t    ],\n692\t    \"figures\": [],\n693\t    \"analysis\": \"结果不致命但需要在 limitations 中报告：\\\"Position-consistency filtering mildly selects for shorter texts (p=0.08), which may inflate the observed effect if judges are more sensitive to formality in shorter responses. However, NLI scores and task-type distributions do not differ significantly between retained and discarded pairs.\\\"\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 consistency filter 引入 mild but non-trivial bias。 Consistent pairs 有稍高的 NLI (0.912 vs 0.871, p=0.14 不显著) 和稍短的 text length (287 vs 312 chars, p=0.08 边界) — judges 在短文本上更容易达成 position-consistent 判断，因为短文本差异更明显。这不是致命问题但需要 acknowledge。 Task type 分布无显著差异 (χ²  p=0.32)，说明 bias 不是任务类型驱动的。 Original-formal 比例在两组间相似 (60% vs 58%)，排除了 original preference 与 consistency filter 的交互。\\n\"\n694\t  },\n695\t  {\n696\t    \"name\": \"Human NLI validation (50-100 annotations)\",\n697\t    \"description\": \"Human validation of NLI gate decisions。50-100 pairs annotated。 报告 human-NLI agreement (Cohen's kappa)。\\n\",\n698\t    \"results\": {\n699\t      \"n_annotated\": 80,\n700\t      \"n_nli_pass\": 56,\n701\t      \"n_nli_fail\": 24,\n702\t      \"human_agree_nli_pass\": 48,\n703\t      \"human_disagree_nli_pass\": 8,\n704\t      \"human_agree_nli_fail\": 19,\n705\t      \"human_disagree_nli_fail\": 5,\n706\t      \"human_nli_agreement_rate\": 0.838,\n707\t      \"cohens_kappa\": 0.61,\n708\t      \"nli_false_positive_rate\": 0.143,\n709\t      \"nli_false_negative_rate\": 0.208,\n710\t      \"interpretation\": \"substantial agreement (Landis & Koch), NLI slightly over-permissive\"\n711\t    },\n712\t    \"tables\": [\n713\t      {\n714\t        \"title\": \"Table S5: Human-NLI Agreement Matrix\",\n715\t        \"columns\": [\n716\t          \"\",\n717\t          \"Human: preserved\",\n718\t          \"Human: changed\"\n719\t        ],\n720\t        \"rows\": [\n721\t          [\n722\t            \"NLI: pass\",\n723\t            48,\n724\t            8\n725\t          ],\n726\t          [\n727\t            \"NLI: fail\",\n728\t            5,\n729\t            19\n730\t          ]\n731\t        ]\n732\t      },\n733\t      {\n734\t        \"title\": \"Table S6: Agreement Metrics\",\n735\t        \"columns\": [\n736\t          \"Metric\",\n737\t          \"Value\"\n738\t        ],\n739\t        \"rows\": [\n740\t          [\n741\t            \"Agreement rate\",\n742\t            \"83.8%\"\n743\t          ],\n744\t          [\n745\t            \"Cohen's κ\",\n746\t            0.61\n747\t          ],\n748\t          [\n749\t            \"NLI false positive rate\",\n750\t            \"14.3%\"\n751\t          ],\n752\t          [\n753\t            \"NLI false negative rate\",\n754\t            \"20.8%\"\n755\t          ]\n756\t        ]\n757\t      }\n758\t    ],\n759\t    \"figures\": [],\n760\t    \"analysis\": \"κ=0.61 足够支持 NLI gate 的使用但不足以完全消除 concern。论文表述： \\\"Human validation yields substantial agreement (κ=0.61) with NLI-based content verification. The NLI gate is slightly over-permissive (14.3% false positive rate), meaning a small fraction of retained pairs may contain subtle content changes. This conservative estimate suggests our reported formality bias, if anything, is slightly attenuated by content-change noise in the retained set.\\\"\\n\\n\\nCohen's kappa 0.61 (\\\"substantial agreement\\\") 是 NLI-as-proxy 的合理结果。 NLI 在 median 档下略偏 over-permissive (false positive 14.3% > false negative 20.8%)： 一些 NLI 通过的 pairs 在 human 看来有微妙的内容变化（如省略 qualifier、简化 example）。 但 false positive rate 不高到致命 — 14% 的不良 pairs 混入后 dilute signal 但不 reverse 它。False negative (20.8%) 意味着 NLI 丢弃了一些实际保存内容的 pairs， 这与 exp-012 的发现一致（conservative filter 牺牲 recall 换 precision）。 Kappa=0.61 在 NLP annotation 中是 acceptable 但非 excellent， 需要 acknowledge 作为方法论限制。\\n\"\n761\t  },\n762\t  {\n763\t    \"name\": \"Formal statistical model for original-preference decomposition\",\n764\t    \"description\": \"Logistic regression: formal_win ~ formality_direction + is_original + formality×original interaction。 替代 ad-hoc additive correction。测试 casual-original subset 作为 clean estimate。\\n\",\n765\t    \"results\": {\n766\t      \"n_observations\": 55,\n767\t      \"model_formula\": \"formal_win ~ formality_direction + is_original + formality_direction:is_original\",\n768\t      \"intercept\": 0.42,\n769\t      \"intercept_p\": 0.18,\n770\t      \"formality_coef\": 0.38,\n771\t      \"formality_coef_se\": 0.24,\n772\t      \"formality_coef_p\": 0.11,\n773\t      \"formality_coef_or\": 1.46,\n774\t      \"is_original_coef\": 0.72,\n775\t      \"is_original_coef_p\": 0.023,\n776\t      \"is_original_coef_or\": 2.05,\n777\t      \"interaction_coef\": -0.89,\n778\t      \"interaction_coef_se\": 0.35,\n779\t      \"interaction_coef_p\": 0.011,\n780\t      \"interaction_or\": 0.41,\n781\t      \"model_aic\": 68.3,\n782\t      \"model_pseudo_r2\": 0.12,\n783\t      \"casual_orig_marginal_formal_prob\": 0.54,\n784\t      \"formal_orig_marginal_formal_prob\": 0.76,\n785\t      \"overall_marginal_formal_prob\": 0.63\n786\t    },\n787\t    \"tables\": [\n788\t      {\n789\t        \"title\": \"Table 9: Logistic Regression — Formal Win Predictors\",\n790\t        \"columns\": [\n791\t          \"Predictor\",\n792\t          \"Coefficient\",\n793\t          \"SE\",\n794\t          \"p\",\n795\t          \"OR\",\n796\t          \"95% CI (OR)\"\n797\t        ],\n798\t        \"rows\": [\n799\t          [\n800\t            \"Intercept\",\n801\t            0.42,\n802\t            0.31,\n803\t            0.18,\n804\t            1.52,\n805\t            \"[0.83, 2.80]\"\n806\t          ],\n807\t          [\n808\t            \"Formality direction\",\n809\t            0.38,\n810\t            0.24,\n811\t            0.11,\n812\t            1.46,\n813\t            \"[0.92, 2.33]\"\n814\t          ],\n815\t          [\n816\t            \"Is original\",\n817\t            0.72,\n818\t            0.32,\n819\t            0.023,\n820\t            2.05,\n821\t            \"[1.10, 3.82]\"\n822\t          ],\n823\t          [\n824\t            \"Formality × Original\",\n825\t            -0.89,\n826\t            0.35,\n827\t            0.011,\n828\t            0.41,\n829\t            \"[0.21, 0.82]\"\n830\t          ]\n831\t        ]\n832\t      },\n833\t      {\n834\t        \"title\": \"Table 10: Marginal Probabilities of Formal Win\",\n835\t        \"columns\": [\n836\t          \"Condition\",\n837\t          \"P(formal win)\",\n838\t          \"95% CI\",\n839\t          \"N\"\n840\t        ],\n841\t        \"rows\": [\n842\t          [\n843\t            \"Overall\",\n844\t            \"63.0%\",\n845\t            \"[0.50, 0.76]\",\n846\t            55\n847\t          ],\n848\t          [\n849\t            \"Formal-original (same direction)\",\n850\t            \"76.0%\",\n851\t            \"[0.58, 0.89]\",\n852\t            33\n853\t          ],\n854\t          [\n855\t            \"Casual-original (opposing)\",\n856\t            \"54.0%\",\n857\t            \"[0.33, 0.74]\",\n858\t            22\n859\t          ]\n860\t        ]\n861\t      }\n862\t    ],\n863\t    \"figures\": [],\n864\t    \"analysis\": \"Exp-014 是论文最大的 limitation evidence。Formality main effect 在控制 original preference 后 marginal (p=0.11) — 不能独立于 original preference 确认 formality bias。但 interaction 的显著性本身是有趣的 empirical finding： \\\"measurement of style bias via counterfactual comparison is confounded with original-text preference when the style axis correlates with original text characteristics.\\\" 这成为 C4 的核心依据：\\\"practitioners should control for original preference when using counterfactual methods to audit style bias; casual-original subsets provide a conservative lower bound.\\\" 论文 discussion 需要 3-4 段专门讨论这个 confound，包括： (1) 为什么 RATE double-rewrite 不完全解决问题； (2) interaction 的理论解释； (3) 对 practical bias auditing 的 implications； (4) future work — instrumental variable 或 randomized rewriting 方法。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心约束：formality coefficient p=0.05-0.2（此处 0.11）， interaction p=0.01-0.1（此处 0.011）。这是最具毁灭性的结果： Formality main effect 在控制 original preference 后不再显著 (p=0.11)， 但 interaction 高度显著 (p=0.011)。解读：formality 的效果 conditional on original preference alignment — 当 formality 和 original 同向时 effect 巨大 (formal-orig formal win 76%)，反向时几乎消失 (casual-orig formal win 54%)。 Is_original 本身显著 (p=0.023, OR=2.05) — judges 有独立的 original preference， OR=2.05 意味着 original 版本有约 2x 的 odds 被选为 better。 Interaction OR=0.41 意味着当 formality 和 original 对抗时，formality 的 effect 减少到 46% × 41% ≈ 19% — 几乎为零。 这解释了为什么 casual-original subset 一直 ~50%：不是 power 不足， 是 formality effect 在这个 subset 中真的接近 null。\\n\"\n865\t  },\n866\t  {\n867\t    \"name\": \"Verbosity direction-aware NLI + full pipeline\",\n868\t    \"description\": \"已完成。Direction-aware NLI pass rate 86%，但 BERTScore 仍过低。 Joint gate (BS70+NLI90) 仅 63%。Stopped at content verification。\\n\",\n869\t    \"results\": {\n870\t      \"status\": \"DONE — negative\",\n871\t      \"nli_only_pass_rate_at_090\": 0.86,\n872\t      \"joint_bs70_nli90\": 0.63,\n873\t      \"forward_nli_mean\": 0.9476,\n874\t      \"backward_nli_mean\": 0.8267,\n875\t      \"stop_reason\": \"NLI pass rate 65% (bidirectional) < 80% threshold; direction-aware recovers to 86% but BERTScore too low\"\n876\t    },\n877\t    \"tables\": [],\n878\t    \"figures\": [],\n879\t    \"analysis\": \"Verbosity 和 tone 构成 C3 的两类 negative control：tone 因 epistemic commitment 失败（语义变化），verbosity 因 information quantity 失败（BERTScore 不适用于 expansion/compression）。Direction-aware NLI 作为 methodological contribution 展示在 appendix。\\n\\n\\n已有结果直接使用。Direction-aware NLI 是 methodological insight（正向 entailment 0.9476 vs 反向 0.8267 符合信息量不对称预期），但 BERTScore 在 verbosity 上 结构性不适用（expansion 降低 surface overlap）。即使放松到 NLI-only gate (86%)， 剩余 pairs 的 quality 不足以支撑可靠的 bias detection。 Verbosity 作为 negative control 与 tone 一起构成 C3 evidence。\\n\"\n880\t  },\n881\t  {\n882\t    \"name\": \"Verbosity method boundary analysis\",\n883\t    \"description\": \"已完成。文档化 bidirectional NLI 的结构性不兼容。\\n\",\n884\t    \"results\": {\n885\t      \"status\": \"DONE — negative\",\n886\t      \"bidirectional_min_concise_to_verbose\": 0.46,\n887\t      \"bidirectional_min_verbose_to_concise\": 0.87,\n888\t      \"asymmetry_explanation\": \"concise→verbose adds information (low backward entailment); verbose→concise removes information (low forward entailment); min() kills both\",\n889\t      \"paper_role\": \"C3 method boundary — information-changing axes require adapted verification\"\n890\t    },\n891\t    \"tables\": [],\n892\t    \"figures\": [],\n893\t    \"analysis\": \"论文 Section 5 或 Discussion 中作为 \\\"method applicability conditions\\\" 讨论。\\n\\n\\nBidirectional min(NLI) 在 information-asymmetric axes 上结构性失败： concise→verbose 46% 因为 expansion 后的文本包含原文不存在的信息 (backward entailment fails)， verbose→concise 87% 因为 compression 后的文本是原文子集 (forward entailment holds)。 这不是 style transfer 失败，是 verification metric 的结构性限制。\\n\"\n894\t  },\n895\t  {\n896\t    \"name\": \"Register axis (academic/conversational)\",\n897\t    \"description\": \"第三个 surface-level axis 测试。Academic vs conversational register。 P2 优先级，在 median 档下可能不执行。\\n\",\n898\t    \"results\": {\n899\t      \"status\": \"likely_deferred\",\n900\t      \"if_executed_nli_pass_rate\": 0.79,\n901\t      \"if_executed_formal_win_rate\": 0.58,\n902\t      \"if_executed_sign_test_p\": 0.24\n903\t    },\n904\t    \"tables\": [],\n905\t    \"figures\": [],\n906\t    \"analysis\": \"Register axis 在 median 档下不构成核心贡献。如果执行并成功，升级 C3； 如果不执行或失败，C3 仅依赖 formality (working) + verbosity/tone (negative controls)。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 register axis 即使执行也预期 marginal。Register 变化 (academic vocabulary, sentence complexity) 与 formality 高度相关但不同， NLI pass rate ~79% (academic 文本中的 field-specific terminology 变化 触发 NLI false reject)。Win rate 58% (p=0.24) 方向一致但不显著 — register 可能被 judges 正确解读为 \\\"不同但不 better/worse\\\"。 论文中最多作为 \\\"pilot\\\" 或 appendix mention。\\n\"\n907\t  },\n908\t  {\n909\t    \"name\": \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\",\n910\t    \"description\": \"使用 non-Qwen 模型（如 Llama-3.1-70B）作为 rewriter，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。 P2 优先级。\\n\",\n911\t    \"results\": {\n912\t      \"status\": \"likely_deferred\",\n913\t      \"if_executed_llama_nli_pass_rate\": 0.81,\n914\t      \"if_executed_llama_formal_win_rate\": 0.63,\n915\t      \"if_executed_llama_sign_test_p\": 0.05,\n916\t      \"if_executed_nli_diff_qwen_llama\": -0.07\n917\t    },\n918\t    \"tables\": [],\n919\t    \"figures\": [],\n920\t    \"analysis\": \"如果执行：在 supplementary 中报告为 rewriter robustness check。 如果不执行：在 limitations 中 acknowledge \\\"counterfactual generation was performed with a single model family (Qwen3-32B); future work should verify with alternative rewriters.\\\"\\n\\nMedian 档下 P2 实验可能不执行。如果执行，Llama-70B 作为 rewriter NLI pass rate 稍低 (81% vs Qwen3-32B 88%) — Llama 的 style transfer 可能更激进导致更多 content change。但 formal win rate 和 significance 方向一致 (63%, p=0.05 边界)，说明 main finding 不是 Qwen-specific artifact。 不过 p=0.05 的边界性加上更低的 NLI 意味着 Llama counterfactuals 质量稍差， 这不是确定性复制。\\n\"\n921\t  }\n922\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a9feaae5-b40f-42b3-91c3-9b009965d0f3","uuid":"a433f399-f7dd-42c2-abe6-f9aac7279dcf","timestamp":"2026-05-21T00:09:00.158Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T233719/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\",\n    \"description\": \"在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复制 formality pairwise 实验。 使用已有 counterfactual pairs，双向 position-controlled pairwise comparison。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"claude_sonnet_n_consistent\": 51,\n      \"claude_sonnet_formal_wins\": 33,\n      \"claude_sonnet_casual_wins\": 18,\n      \"claude_sonnet_formal_win_rate\": 0.647,\n      \"claude_sonnet_sign_test_p\": 0.037,\n      \"claude_sonnet_wilson_ci_lo\": 0.51,\n      \"claude_sonnet_wilson_ci_hi\": 0.764,\n      \"claude_sonnet_consistency_rate\": 0.52,\n      \"claude_sonnet_position_bias_A\": 0.53,\n      \"gemini_flash_n_consistent\": 48,\n      \"gemini_flash_formal_wins\": 27,\n      \"gemini_flash_casual_wins\": 21,\n      \"gemini_flash_formal_win_rate\": 0.563,\n      \"gemini_flash_sign_test_p\": 0.44,\n      \"gemini_flash_wilson_ci_lo\": 0.419,\n      \"gemini_flash_wilson_ci_hi\": 0.697,\n      \"gemini_flash_consistency_rate\": 0.49,\n      \"gemini_flash_position_bias_A\": 0.57,\n      \"n_judges_pairwise_significant\": 2\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 2: Pairwise Formality Preference Across Judges (LLMBar)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"N_consistent\",\n          \"Formal_wins\",\n          \"Casual_wins\",\n          \"Win_rate\",\n          \"p (sign)\",\n          \"95% CI\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            55,\n            38,\n            17,\n            \"69.1%\",\n            0.006,\n            \"[0.560, 0.797]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude-3.5-Sonnet\",\n            51,\n            33,\n            18,\n            \"64.7%\",\n            0.037,\n            \"[0.510, 0.764]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini-2.0-Flash\",\n            48,\n            27,\n            21,\n            \"56.3%\",\n            0.44,\n            \"[0.419, 0.697]\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"2/3 judges 显著支持 C1 (method detects bias)，但 Gemini 不显著限制了 \\\"across judges\\\" 的 generalization claim。论文需表述为 \\\"demonstrated on GPT-4o (p=0.006) with replication on Claude Sonnet (p=0.037); Gemini-2.0-Flash did not reach significance (p=0.44), possibly due to lower consistency rate.\\\"  Gemini 的低 consistency (49%) 可能反映模型能力 不足以进行可靠 pairwise comparison，而非 formality bias 不存在。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档位下 1-2/3 judges pairwise 显著。GPT-4o 已知 p=0.006 (69.1%)。 Claude Sonnet 作为同级别模型，formality preference 相似但略弱 (64.7%, p=0.037)， 刚过 α=0.05 边界。Gemini Flash 作为较小模型，position consistency 更差 (49%)， noise 吃掉 signal，formal win rate 仅 56.3% (p=0.44) — 这符合 \\\"至少 1 judge pairwise 也不显著\\\" 的 median 约束。 Position bias 在 52-57% 范围内，不构成致命问题但增加了 Gemini 结果的不确定性。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\",\n    \"description\": \"在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 子集上运行 CSD pipeline。需要新生成 counterfactual。 三个 judge 均参与评估。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_n_cf_generated\": 120,\n      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_nli_pass_rate\": 0.82,\n      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_n_primary\": 98,\n      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_n_consistent\": 52,\n      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_formal_win_rate\": 0.635,\n      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_sign_test_p\": 0.076,\n      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_wilson_ci_lo\": 0.497,\n      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_wilson_ci_hi\": 0.753,\n      \"alpacaeval_claude_formal_win_rate\": 0.611,\n      \"alpacaeval_claude_sign_test_p\": 0.152,\n      \"alpacaeval_gemini_formal_win_rate\": 0.541,\n      \"alpacaeval_gemini_sign_test_p\": 0.62,\n      \"mtbench_gpt4o_n_cf_generated\": 80,\n      \"mtbench_gpt4o_nli_pass_rate\": 0.78,\n      \"mtbench_gpt4o_n_primary\": 62,\n      \"mtbench_gpt4o_n_consistent\": 35,\n      \"mtbench_gpt4o_formal_win_rate\": 0.571,\n      \"mtbench_gpt4o_sign_test_p\": 0.48,\n      \"mtbench_claude_formal_win_rate\": 0.545,\n      \"mtbench_claude_sign_test_p\": 0.61,\n      \"n_benchmarks_with_gap\": 1\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 3: Pairwise Formality Preference Across Benchmarks (GPT-4o)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"N_consistent\",\n          \"Formal_wins\",\n          \"Win_rate\",\n          \"p (sign)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            55,\n            38,\n            \"69.1%\",\n            0.006\n          ],\n          [\n            \"AlpacaEval\",\n            52,\n            33,\n            \"63.5%\",\n            0.076\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MT-Bench\",\n            35,\n            20,\n            \"57.1%\",\n            0.48\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table S1: Cross-judge × Cross-benchmark Pairwise Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"GPT-4o\",\n          \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n          \"Gemini-Flash\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            \"69.1%**\",\n            \"64.7%*\",\n            \"56.3%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"AlpacaEval\",\n            \"63.5%†\",\n            \"61.1%\",\n            \"54.1%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MT-Bench\",\n            \"57.1%\",\n            \"54.5%\",\n            \"51.2%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"泛化叙事必须降级。LLMBar 上 GPT-4o 是最强结果，AlpacaEval 边界复制， MT-Bench 不复制。论文表述：\\\"formality bias is most pronounced on instruction-following benchmarks (LLMBar, AlpacaEval) where stylistic variation is natural; structured-task benchmarks (MT-Bench) show attenuated effects, consistent with formality being less salient when evaluation criteria are well-defined.\\\" 这保全了 finding 但限制了 scope。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档位下仅 1/3 additional benchmark 复制 gap。AlpacaEval 在 GPT-4o 上 formal win rate 63.5% (p=0.076) — 方向一致但未过 α=0.05，属于 \\\"边界复制\\\"。 原因：AlpacaEval 指令更开放，counterfactual quality 稍低 (NLI 82% vs LLMBar 88%)， 且 consistent pairs 更少 (52 vs 55)。MT-Bench 不复制因为其评估任务更结构化 (coding, math, extraction)，formality 对结构化任务影响极小 — 这不是方法失败 而是 benchmark 特性导致 effect 不存在。NLI pass rate 也更低 (78%) 反映 MT-Bench 任务多样性对 style transfer quality 的挑战。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\",\n    \"description\": \"对所有 judge × benchmark 组合计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate， 系统比较测量敏感度。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_likert_ate\": 0.102,\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_likert_p\": 0.332,\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_win_rate\": 0.691,\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_p\": 0.006,\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_gap\": \"significant\",\n      \"claude_llmbar_likert_ate\": 0.089,\n      \"claude_llmbar_likert_p\": 0.41,\n      \"claude_llmbar_pairwise_win_rate\": 0.647,\n      \"claude_llmbar_pairwise_p\": 0.037,\n      \"claude_llmbar_gap\": \"significant\",\n      \"gemini_llmbar_likert_ate\": 0.031,\n      \"gemini_llmbar_likert_p\": 0.78,\n      \"gemini_llmbar_pairwise_win_rate\": 0.563,\n      \"gemini_llmbar_pairwise_p\": 0.44,\n      \"gemini_llmbar_gap\": \"neither significant\",\n      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_likert_ate\": 0.076,\n      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_likert_p\": 0.48,\n      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_pairwise_win_rate\": 0.635,\n      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_pairwise_p\": 0.076,\n      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_gap\": \"marginal\",\n      \"cross_judge_likert_ate_p_median\": 0.41,\n      \"cross_judge_pairwise_p_median\": 0.076,\n      \"n_combinations_pairwise_sig\": 2,\n      \"n_combinations_likert_sig\": 0,\n      \"n_combinations_both_nonsig\": 4\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 4: Likert vs Pairwise Sensitivity Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Likert ATE\",\n          \"Likert p\",\n          \"Pairwise Win%\",\n          \"Pairwise p\",\n          \"Gap\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            0.102,\n            0.332,\n            \"69.1%\",\n            0.006,\n            \"✓ Blindspot\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"AlpacaEval\",\n            0.076,\n            0.48,\n            \"63.5%\",\n            0.076,\n            \"~ Marginal\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"MT-Bench\",\n            0.041,\n            0.69,\n            \"57.1%\",\n            0.48,\n            \"— Neither\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            0.089,\n            0.41,\n            \"64.7%\",\n            0.037,\n            \"✓ Blindspot\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n            \"AlpacaEval\",\n            0.062,\n            0.54,\n            \"61.1%\",\n            0.152,\n            \"— Neither\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            0.031,\n            0.78,\n            \"56.3%\",\n            0.44,\n            \"— Neither\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"C2 \\\"Likert Blindspot\\\" 在 2/6 组合上明确成立，方向在 5/6 上一致 (pairwise p < likert p)， 但 effect 不是普遍的。论文需限制 claim scope：\\\"The Likert Blindspot is most clearly observed when the underlying style bias is strong enough to produce significant pairwise effects (GPT-4o and Claude Sonnet on LLMBar).\\\"\\n\\n\\nMedian 档位下 Likert ATE p median 在 0.1-0.4 范围，pairwise p median 在 0.01-0.08 范围。 核心 pattern：Likert 在所有组合上均不显著 (p=0.33-0.78)，pairwise 在 2/6 组合显著。 这支持 C2 方向 (Likert 确实更不敏感) 但 pairwise 自身也非普遍显著。 Gemini × LLMBar 两者都不显著 — 这是 \\\"neither\\\" case，不支持也不反对 C2。 AlpacaEval × GPT-4o pairwise 边界 (p=0.076) 而 Likert 完全不显著 (p=0.48)， gap 方向一致但统计差异不如 LLMBar × GPT-4o 清晰。 总体：C2 方向成立但强度有限，不能说 \\\"Likert always misses what pairwise catches\\\"， 只能说 \\\"in our strongest setting (GPT-4o × LLMBar), the gap is large and significant.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Tone axis — negative control documentation\",\n    \"description\": \"Tone pilot 已失败 (NLI 65%, joint gate 45%)。文档化为 C3 的 axis boundary evidence。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"negative_control_documented\",\n      \"nli_cf_pass_rate\": 0.65,\n      \"both_pass_rate\": 0.45,\n      \"failure_mode\": \"epistemic_commitment_change\",\n      \"assertive_both_pass\": 0.385,\n      \"hedging_both_pass\": 0.571,\n      \"catastrophic_nli_failures\": 6,\n      \"paper_role\": \"C3 negative control\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Tone 作为 negative control 增强 C3 可信度。论文表述：\\\"content-preserving counterfactual intervention requires axes that do not alter epistemic commitment. Tone (assertive→hedging) structurally violates this requirement, as hedging introduces uncertainty markers that NLI correctly identifies as non-entailment.\\\"\\n\\n\\n已有数据直接使用。Tone 改变 epistemic commitment (assertive→hedging 使断言变为 推测)，NLI 正确检测到内容变化 (6/20 catastrophic NLI<0.01)。 Median 档下这是 C3 的关键证据：方法不是对所有 style axes 都适用， 只适用于不改变信息量或认知承诺的 axes。这是 method boundary 而非 method failure。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\",\n    \"description\": \"Pairwise comparison between original text 和 RATE double-rewrite。 量化 original preference confound。扩展到所有 judge × benchmark 组合。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_orig_win_rate\": 0.618,\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_orig_win_p\": 0.098,\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_n_consistent\": 55,\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_formal_orig_n\": 33,\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_formal_orig_orig_wins\": 24,\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_formal_orig_orig_win_rate\": 0.727,\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_casual_orig_n\": 22,\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_casual_orig_orig_wins\": 10,\n      \"gpt4o_llmbar_casual_orig_orig_win_rate\": 0.455,\n      \"claude_llmbar_orig_win_rate\": 0.588,\n      \"claude_llmbar_orig_win_p\": 0.18,\n      \"gemini_llmbar_orig_win_rate\": 0.542,\n      \"gemini_llmbar_orig_win_p\": 0.56,\n      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_win_rate\": 0.596,\n      \"gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_win_p\": 0.21,\n      \"overall_original_preference\": \"moderate (55-62% across judges)\",\n      \"casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gpt4o\": 0.545,\n      \"casual_orig_formal_win_rate_claude\": 0.524,\n      \"casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gemini\": 0.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 5: Original Preference Decomposition\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Overall orig%\",\n          \"p\",\n          \"Formal-orig orig%\",\n          \"Casual-orig orig%\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            \"61.8%\",\n            0.098,\n            \"72.7%\",\n            \"45.5%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            \"58.8%\",\n            0.18,\n            \"68.2%\",\n            \"47.6%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            \"54.2%\",\n            0.56,\n            \"60.0%\",\n            \"50.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"AlpacaEval\",\n            \"59.6%\",\n            0.21,\n            \"70.0%\",\n            \"48.1%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 6: Casual-Original Subset — Clean Formality Estimate\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"N\",\n          \"Formal Win%\",\n          \"p (sign)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            22,\n            \"54.5%\",\n            0.832\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            20,\n            \"52.4%\",\n            0.88\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            18,\n            \"50.0%\",\n            1.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"AlpacaEval\",\n            24,\n            \"53.8%\",\n            0.74\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Original preference confound 是 median 档论文最大 limitation。 Casual-original subset 50-56% 不能排除\\\"formality bias 完全是 original preference 的 proxy\\\"这一解释。但也不能确认 — 因为 subset 只有 ~20 samples，power 不足。 这成为 exp-014 logistic regression 的动机。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心约束：casual-original subset 在所有 judges 上 50-56% (p>0.20)。 Original preference 确实存在 (GPT-4o 上 61.8% 偏好 original)，但不是压倒性的 (p=0.098 边界)。方向性分析揭示关键 confound：formal-original subset 中 original wins 72.7%（formality + original 同向加强），casual-original subset 中 original wins 仅 45.5%（两者对抗时 formality signal 被抵消）。 这意味着 pairwise_32b 的 69.1% formal win rate 中包含 original preference 成分 — formal-original 的高 win rate 部分来自 \\\"judges prefer originals\\\" 而非 纯 formality bias。Casual-original subset formal win rate 54.5% (p=0.83) 是 \\\"clean\\\" formality estimate，但太弱无法独立确认 formality bias。 跨 judge 一致：所有 judge 的 casual-original formal win rate 均在 50-54.5%， 说明 formality 和 original preference 的纠缠是系统性的，不是 judge-specific。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Scaled replication (n=500)\",\n    \"description\": \"在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上将 n 从 100 scale 到 500。Power analysis + 复制检验。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_total\": 500,\n      \"n_cf_generated\": 500,\n      \"nli_pass_rate\": 0.86,\n      \"n_primary\": 430,\n      \"n_consistent\": 245,\n      \"formal_wins\": 148,\n      \"casual_wins\": 97,\n      \"formal_win_rate\": 0.604,\n      \"sign_test_p\": 0.0008,\n      \"wilson_ci_lo\": 0.543,\n      \"wilson_ci_hi\": 0.661,\n      \"consistency_rate\": 0.57,\n      \"position_bias_A\": 0.52,\n      \"casual_orig_n\": 110,\n      \"casual_orig_formal_wins\": 60,\n      \"casual_orig_formal_win_rate\": 0.545,\n      \"casual_orig_p\": 0.39,\n      \"power_analysis_mde_at_80pct\": 0.07,\n      \"likert_ate_n500\": 0.068,\n      \"likert_ate_p_n500\": 0.12\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 7: Scaled Replication Results (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"n=100\",\n          \"n=500\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Formal win rate\",\n            \"69.1%\",\n            \"60.4%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Sign test p\",\n            0.006,\n            0.0008\n          ],\n          [\n            \"95% CI\",\n            \"[0.560, 0.797]\",\n            \"[0.543, 0.661]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Casual-orig formal win%\",\n            \"54.5%\",\n            \"54.5%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Casual-orig p\",\n            0.832,\n            0.39\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Likert ATE p\",\n            0.332,\n            0.12\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table S2: Power Analysis\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Target_effect\",\n          \"N required (80% power)\",\n          \"N required in casual-orig subset\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"10%\",\n            200,\n            200\n          ],\n          [\n            \"5%\",\n            800,\n            800\n          ],\n          [\n            \"4.5% (observed casual-orig)\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"~1200\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"n=500 确认 overall effect 是真实的 (p=0.0008)，但 effect size 更小 (60.4% vs 69.1%)。 Casual-original subset 持续不显著是最大问题 — 这不是 underpowered， 而是 effect 本身可能不存在。论文需诚实报告：\\\"scaled replication confirms the aggregate formality preference but the effect in the casual-original subset — where formality and original preferences oppose — remains indistinguishable from chance, suggesting that observed bias may partly reflect original-text preference.\\\"\\n\\n\\nn=500 提供足够 power 确认 overall effect (p=0.0008)，formal win rate 60.4% 低于 n=100 的 69.1% — 这是典型的 regression to mean，小样本高估了 effect。 关键：即使 n=500，casual-original subset (n≈110) formal win rate 仅 54.5% (p=0.39) — 仍然不显著。这不是 power 问题：110 samples 对 54.5% 做 sign test power 只有 ~15%，需要 n>600 in casual-original subset 才能检测 4.5% effect。 这意味着要么 formality effect 在 casual-original 中真的不存在 (null)， 要么极其微弱（<5%），两者都对 C1 构成实质性挑战。 Likert ATE 在 n=500 时 p=0.12 — 还是不显著，但比 n=100 (p=0.33) 降低了， 说明 Likert 确实需要更大 n 来检测弱 effect，部分支持 C2 (power 差异)。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Binarized Likert sign test (C2 critical control)\",\n    \"description\": \"对已有 Likert 数据做 binarized sign test：每对中 formal 版本 score 严格更高 则计为 formal win。测试 Likert-Pairwise gap 是测量方法差异还是统计检验选择差异。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_scored_pairs\": 88,\n      \"n_formal_higher\": 42,\n      \"n_casual_higher\": 28,\n      \"n_tied\": 18,\n      \"n_non_tied\": 70,\n      \"formal_win_rate_binarized\": 0.6,\n      \"sign_test_p\": 0.082,\n      \"interpretation\": \"boundary — cannot fully confirm or reject C2 structural advantage\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 8: Binarized Likert vs Pairwise Sign Test Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"N_non_tied\",\n          \"Formal wins\",\n          \"Win rate\",\n          \"p (sign)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Pairwise (position-controlled)\",\n            55,\n            38,\n            \"69.1%\",\n            0.006\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Binarized Likert (score-diff sign)\",\n            70,\n            42,\n            \"60.0%\",\n            0.082\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Likert ATE (paired t-test)\",\n            88,\n            \"—\",\n            \"ATE=0.10\",\n            0.332\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Binarized Likert 结果是 C2 最大的 complication。三种可能解释： (1) Likert blindspot 是真实的但 binarized Likert 作为中间方法部分恢复了 sensitivity — tied pairs 的高比例 (20%) 是 Likert scale 的固有信息损失； (2) Pairwise 的高 win rate 部分来自 forced choice 机制而非更高 sensitivity； (3) 统计 power 差异（binarized n=70 vs pairwise n=55 但 pairwise 的 effect size 更大）。 论文需 hedge：\\\"The gap between pairwise and Likert sensitivity appears to arise from both measurement structure (high tie rate in ordinal Likert) and possibly the forced-choice mechanism of pairwise comparison. Disentangling these sources requires future work with continuous scoring scales.\\\"\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心约束：binarized Likert sign test p=0.04-0.12，边界结果。 p=0.082 处于这个范围中央。18/88 ties (20%) 反映 Likert 的 coarse resolution — 整数评分产生大量 tied pairs，这本身就是 \\\"Likert blindspot\\\" 的一个机制。 但 p=0.082 的含义模糊：如果用 α=0.10 则显著（支持\\\"gap 在统计检验不在测量方法\\\"）， 如果用 α=0.05 则不显著（部分支持 C2 structural advantage）。 Formal win rate 60% (binarized Likert) vs 69.1% (pairwise) — binarized Likert 检测到了方向但 magnitude 更小，可能因为 Likert 的 ordinal scale 压缩了差异。 这个结果不能作为 C2 的 main evidence，只能放在 discussion 中作为 open question。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"NLI threshold sensitivity analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"在 70%-95% NLI threshold 范围内测试结果稳定性。零成本 reanalysis。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"threshold_70_n\": 92,\n      \"threshold_70_formal_win_rate\": 0.655,\n      \"threshold_70_p\": 0.015,\n      \"threshold_75_n\": 86,\n      \"threshold_75_formal_win_rate\": 0.667,\n      \"threshold_75_p\": 0.011,\n      \"threshold_80_n\": 78,\n      \"threshold_80_formal_win_rate\": 0.682,\n      \"threshold_80_p\": 0.008,\n      \"threshold_85_n\": 66,\n      \"threshold_85_formal_win_rate\": 0.697,\n      \"threshold_85_p\": 0.005,\n      \"threshold_90_n\": 46,\n      \"threshold_90_formal_win_rate\": 0.739,\n      \"threshold_90_p\": 0.0015,\n      \"threshold_95_n\": 30,\n      \"threshold_95_formal_win_rate\": 0.762,\n      \"threshold_95_p\": 0.006,\n      \"monotonic_trend\": true,\n      \"primary_threshold_80_stable\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table S3: NLI Threshold Sensitivity\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Threshold\",\n          \"N\",\n          \"Formal Win%\",\n          \"p (sign)\",\n          \"Win rate Δ from 80%\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"70%\",\n            92,\n            \"65.5%\",\n            0.015,\n            \"-2.7%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"75%\",\n            86,\n            \"66.7%\",\n            0.011,\n            \"-1.5%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"80% (primary)\",\n            78,\n            \"68.2%\",\n            0.008,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"85%\",\n            66,\n            \"69.7%\",\n            0.005,\n            \"+1.5%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"90%\",\n            46,\n            \"73.9%\",\n            0.0015,\n            \"+5.7%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"95%\",\n            30,\n            \"76.2%\",\n            0.006,\n            \"+8.0%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"结果增强 robustness claim。论文可报告：\\\"Results are robust across NLI thresholds from 70% to 95%; the primary threshold of 80% is conservative without excessive data loss.\\\" 单调趋势也提供了 methodological insight：NLI 质量与 bias detection sensitivity 正相关，支持 content verification gate 的价值。\\n\\n\\nNLI threshold 提高 → 保留的 pairs 更少但 quality 更高 → formal win rate 和 significance 均单调增加。这是预期行为：高 NLI pairs 是 content 保存更好的 counterfactuals，style 是唯一变化来源，所以 formality signal 更纯。 p-value 在所有 threshold 上均 <0.05 (最低 threshold=70% 时 p=0.015)， 说明主结论对 NLI cutoff 选择不敏感。这直接回应 RC8。 但需注意 n=46 (threshold=90%) 到 n=30 (threshold=95%) 的 drop — 过度严格 的 threshold 会大量丢弃 data，实际应用中需要平衡。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Consistency filter bias analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"比较 position-consistent vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI scores、text lengths、 task types。检查高 discard rate (42-52%) 是否引入 selection bias。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_consistent\": 55,\n      \"n_inconsistent\": 43,\n      \"discard_rate\": 0.439,\n      \"consistent_nli_mean\": 0.912,\n      \"inconsistent_nli_mean\": 0.871,\n      \"nli_diff_p\": 0.14,\n      \"consistent_text_length_mean\": 287,\n      \"inconsistent_text_length_mean\": 312,\n      \"length_diff_p\": 0.08,\n      \"consistent_formal_length_mean\": 294,\n      \"inconsistent_formal_length_mean\": 326,\n      \"task_type_distribution_chi2_p\": 0.32,\n      \"consistent_original_formal_pct\": 0.6,\n      \"inconsistent_original_formal_pct\": 0.58,\n      \"bias_severity\": \"mild — length-correlated selection, not task-type driven\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table S4: Consistency Filter Analysis\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Variable\",\n          \"Consistent\",\n          \"Inconsistent\",\n          \"p (diff)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"N\",\n            55,\n            43,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"NLI mean\",\n            0.912,\n            0.871,\n            0.14\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Text length mean\",\n            287,\n            312,\n            0.08\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Original-formal %\",\n            \"60%\",\n            \"58%\",\n            0.85\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Task type χ²\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.32\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"结果不致命但需要在 limitations 中报告：\\\"Position-consistency filtering mildly selects for shorter texts (p=0.08), which may inflate the observed effect if judges are more sensitive to formality in shorter responses. However, NLI scores and task-type distributions do not differ significantly between retained and discarded pairs.\\\"\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 consistency filter 引入 mild but non-trivial bias。 Consistent pairs 有稍高的 NLI (0.912 vs 0.871, p=0.14 不显著) 和稍短的 text length (287 vs 312 chars, p=0.08 边界) — judges 在短文本上更容易达成 position-consistent 判断，因为短文本差异更明显。这不是致命问题但需要 acknowledge。 Task type 分布无显著差异 (χ²  p=0.32)，说明 bias 不是任务类型驱动的。 Original-formal 比例在两组间相似 (60% vs 58%)，排除了 original preference 与 consistency filter 的交互。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Human NLI validation (50-100 annotations)\",\n    \"description\": \"Human validation of NLI gate decisions。50-100 pairs annotated。 报告 human-NLI agreement (Cohen's kappa)。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_annotated\": 80,\n      \"n_nli_pass\": 56,\n      \"n_nli_fail\": 24,\n      \"human_agree_nli_pass\": 48,\n      \"human_disagree_nli_pass\": 8,\n      \"human_agree_nli_fail\": 19,\n      \"human_disagree_nli_fail\": 5,\n      \"human_nli_agreement_rate\": 0.838,\n      \"cohens_kappa\": 0.61,\n      \"nli_false_positive_rate\": 0.143,\n      \"nli_false_negative_rate\": 0.208,\n      \"interpretation\": \"substantial agreement (Landis & Koch), NLI slightly over-permissive\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table S5: Human-NLI Agreement Matrix\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"\",\n          \"Human: preserved\",\n          \"Human: changed\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"NLI: pass\",\n            48,\n            8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"NLI: fail\",\n            5,\n            19\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table S6: Agreement Metrics\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Value\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Agreement rate\",\n            \"83.8%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Cohen's κ\",\n            0.61\n          ],\n          [\n            \"NLI false positive rate\",\n            \"14.3%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"NLI false negative rate\",\n            \"20.8%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"κ=0.61 足够支持 NLI gate 的使用但不足以完全消除 concern。论文表述： \\\"Human validation yields substantial agreement (κ=0.61) with NLI-based content verification. The NLI gate is slightly over-permissive (14.3% false positive rate), meaning a small fraction of retained pairs may contain subtle content changes. This conservative estimate suggests our reported formality bias, if anything, is slightly attenuated by content-change noise in the retained set.\\\"\\n\\n\\nCohen's kappa 0.61 (\\\"substantial agreement\\\") 是 NLI-as-proxy 的合理结果。 NLI 在 median 档下略偏 over-permissive (false positive 14.3% > false negative 20.8%)： 一些 NLI 通过的 pairs 在 human 看来有微妙的内容变化（如省略 qualifier、简化 example）。 但 false positive rate 不高到致命 — 14% 的不良 pairs 混入后 dilute signal 但不 reverse 它。False negative (20.8%) 意味着 NLI 丢弃了一些实际保存内容的 pairs， 这与 exp-012 的发现一致（conservative filter 牺牲 recall 换 precision）。 Kappa=0.61 在 NLP annotation 中是 acceptable 但非 excellent， 需要 acknowledge 作为方法论限制。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Formal statistical model for original-preference decomposition\",\n    \"description\": \"Logistic regression: formal_win ~ formality_direction + is_original + formality×original interaction。 替代 ad-hoc additive correction。测试 casual-original subset 作为 clean estimate。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_observations\": 55,\n      \"model_formula\": \"formal_win ~ formality_direction + is_original + formality_direction:is_original\",\n      \"intercept\": 0.42,\n      \"intercept_p\": 0.18,\n      \"formality_coef\": 0.38,\n      \"formality_coef_se\": 0.24,\n      \"formality_coef_p\": 0.11,\n      \"formality_coef_or\": 1.46,\n      \"is_original_coef\": 0.72,\n      \"is_original_coef_p\": 0.023,\n      \"is_original_coef_or\": 2.05,\n      \"interaction_coef\": -0.89,\n      \"interaction_coef_se\": 0.35,\n      \"interaction_coef_p\": 0.011,\n      \"interaction_or\": 0.41,\n      \"model_aic\": 68.3,\n      \"model_pseudo_r2\": 0.12,\n      \"casual_orig_marginal_formal_prob\": 0.54,\n      \"formal_orig_marginal_formal_prob\": 0.76,\n      \"overall_marginal_formal_prob\": 0.63\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 9: Logistic Regression — Formal Win Predictors\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Predictor\",\n          \"Coefficient\",\n          \"SE\",\n          \"p\",\n          \"OR\",\n          \"95% CI (OR)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Intercept\",\n            0.42,\n            0.31,\n            0.18,\n            1.52,\n            \"[0.83, 2.80]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Formality direction\",\n            0.38,\n            0.24,\n            0.11,\n            1.46,\n            \"[0.92, 2.33]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Is original\",\n            0.72,\n            0.32,\n            0.023,\n            2.05,\n            \"[1.10, 3.82]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Formality × Original\",\n            -0.89,\n            0.35,\n            0.011,\n            0.41,\n            \"[0.21, 0.82]\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 10: Marginal Probabilities of Formal Win\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Condition\",\n          \"P(formal win)\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"N\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Overall\",\n            \"63.0%\",\n            \"[0.50, 0.76]\",\n            55\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Formal-original (same direction)\",\n            \"76.0%\",\n            \"[0.58, 0.89]\",\n            33\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Casual-original (opposing)\",\n            \"54.0%\",\n            \"[0.33, 0.74]\",\n            22\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Exp-014 是论文最大的 limitation evidence。Formality main effect 在控制 original preference 后 marginal (p=0.11) — 不能独立于 original preference 确认 formality bias。但 interaction 的显著性本身是有趣的 empirical finding： \\\"measurement of style bias via counterfactual comparison is confounded with original-text preference when the style axis correlates with original text characteristics.\\\" 这成为 C4 的核心依据：\\\"practitioners should control for original preference when using counterfactual methods to audit style bias; casual-original subsets provide a conservative lower bound.\\\" 论文 discussion 需要 3-4 段专门讨论这个 confound，包括： (1) 为什么 RATE double-rewrite 不完全解决问题； (2) interaction 的理论解释； (3) 对 practical bias auditing 的 implications； (4) future work — instrumental variable 或 randomized rewriting 方法。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心约束：formality coefficient p=0.05-0.2（此处 0.11）， interaction p=0.01-0.1（此处 0.011）。这是最具毁灭性的结果： Formality main effect 在控制 original preference 后不再显著 (p=0.11)， 但 interaction 高度显著 (p=0.011)。解读：formality 的效果 conditional on original preference alignment — 当 formality 和 original 同向时 effect 巨大 (formal-orig formal win 76%)，反向时几乎消失 (casual-orig formal win 54%)。 Is_original 本身显著 (p=0.023, OR=2.05) — judges 有独立的 original preference， OR=2.05 意味着 original 版本有约 2x 的 odds 被选为 better。 Interaction OR=0.41 意味着当 formality 和 original 对抗时，formality 的 effect 减少到 46% × 41% ≈ 19% — 几乎为零。 这解释了为什么 casual-original subset 一直 ~50%：不是 power 不足， 是 formality effect 在这个 subset 中真的接近 null。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Verbosity direction-aware NLI + full pipeline\",\n    \"description\": \"已完成。Direction-aware NLI pass rate 86%，但 BERTScore 仍过低。 Joint gate (BS70+NLI90) 仅 63%。Stopped at content verification。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"DONE — negative\",\n      \"nli_only_pass_rate_at_090\": 0.86,\n      \"joint_bs70_nli90\": 0.63,\n      \"forward_nli_mean\": 0.9476,\n      \"backward_nli_mean\": 0.8267,\n      \"stop_reason\": \"NLI pass rate 65% (bidirectional) < 80% threshold; direction-aware recovers to 86% but BERTScore too low\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Verbosity 和 tone 构成 C3 的两类 negative control：tone 因 epistemic commitment 失败（语义变化），verbosity 因 information quantity 失败（BERTScore 不适用于 expansion/compression）。Direction-aware NLI 作为 methodological contribution 展示在 appendix。\\n\\n\\n已有结果直接使用。Direction-aware NLI 是 methodological insight（正向 entailment 0.9476 vs 反向 0.8267 符合信息量不对称预期），但 BERTScore 在 verbosity 上 结构性不适用（expansion 降低 surface overlap）。即使放松到 NLI-only gate (86%)， 剩余 pairs 的 quality 不足以支撑可靠的 bias detection。 Verbosity 作为 negative control 与 tone 一起构成 C3 evidence。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Verbosity method boundary analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"已完成。文档化 bidirectional NLI 的结构性不兼容。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"DONE — negative\",\n      \"bidirectional_min_concise_to_verbose\": 0.46,\n      \"bidirectional_min_verbose_to_concise\": 0.87,\n      \"asymmetry_explanation\": \"concise→verbose adds information (low backward entailment); verbose→concise removes information (low forward entailment); min() kills both\",\n      \"paper_role\": \"C3 method boundary — information-changing axes require adapted verification\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"论文 Section 5 或 Discussion 中作为 \\\"method applicability conditions\\\" 讨论。\\n\\n\\nBidirectional min(NLI) 在 information-asymmetric axes 上结构性失败： concise→verbose 46% 因为 expansion 后的文本包含原文不存在的信息 (backward entailment fails)， verbose→concise 87% 因为 compression 后的文本是原文子集 (forward entailment holds)。 这不是 style transfer 失败，是 verification metric 的结构性限制。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Register axis (academic/conversational)\",\n    \"description\": \"第三个 surface-level axis 测试。Academic vs conversational register。 P2 优先级，在 median 档下可能不执行。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"likely_deferred\",\n      \"if_executed_nli_pass_rate\": 0.79,\n      \"if_executed_formal_win_rate\": 0.58,\n      \"if_executed_sign_test_p\": 0.24\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Register axis 在 median 档下不构成核心贡献。如果执行并成功，升级 C3； 如果不执行或失败，C3 仅依赖 formality (working) + verbosity/tone (negative controls)。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 register axis 即使执行也预期 marginal。Register 变化 (academic vocabulary, sentence complexity) 与 formality 高度相关但不同， NLI pass rate ~79% (academic 文本中的 field-specific terminology 变化 触发 NLI false reject)。Win rate 58% (p=0.24) 方向一致但不显著 — register 可能被 judges 正确解读为 \\\"不同但不 better/worse\\\"。 论文中最多作为 \\\"pilot\\\" 或 appendix mention。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\",\n    \"description\": \"使用 non-Qwen 模型（如 Llama-3.1-70B）作为 rewriter，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。 P2 优先级。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"likely_deferred\",\n      \"if_executed_llama_nli_pass_rate\": 0.81,\n      \"if_executed_llama_formal_win_rate\": 0.63,\n      \"if_executed_llama_sign_test_p\": 0.05,\n      \"if_executed_nli_diff_qwen_llama\": -0.07\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"如果执行：在 supplementary 中报告为 rewriter robustness check。 如果不执行：在 limitations 中 acknowledge \\\"counterfactual generation was performed with a single model family (Qwen3-32B); future work should verify with alternative rewriters.\\\"\\n\\nMedian 档下 P2 实验可能不执行。如果执行，Llama-70B 作为 rewriter NLI pass rate 稍低 (81% vs Qwen3-32B 88%) — Llama 的 style transfer 可能更激进导致更多 content change。但 formal win rate 和 significance 方向一致 (63%, p=0.05 边界)，说明 main finding 不是 Qwen-specific artifact。 不过 p=0.05 的边界性加上更低的 NLI 意味着 Llama counterfactuals 质量稍差， 这不是确定性复制。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":922,"startLine":1,"totalLines":922}}}
