{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016Qcb6SuUNq9zfKBe5nstDy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — causal_style_decomp_judge\n2\t\n3\t> Dream 1 (dream_20260520T211832) 三档均 3.0/6 (Findings)。以下为 D015 修正版。\n4\t\n5\t## Target Venue\n6\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n7\t- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n8\t- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n9\t- Format: Long paper, 8-page main text + unlimited references\n10\t\n11\t## Title (Dream 修正)\n12\t**旧**: \"Causal Style Decomposition Reveals Systematic Style Bias in LLM-as-Judge That Likert Scoring Misses\"\n13\t**新**: \"The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Counterfactual Pairwise Comparison\"\n14\t- 理由：三档审稿人一致认为 \"decomposition\" 和 \"framework\" 过度承诺。新标题聚焦最强发现 (C2) 且更准确。\n15\t\n16\t## Core Claims (3 条 + 1 practical，修正后)\n17\t\n18\t### C1 (Method — 降级表述): Counterfactual pairwise comparison 可以 post-hoc 检测 black-box LLM judge 的 style bias\n19\t- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：不是新 \"framework\"，是已知组件（counterfactual rewriting + NLI verification + pairwise comparison）的新应用。论文中必须明确 acknowledge 组件来源（RATE, style transfer evaluation, MT-Bench pairwise）并定位为 application contribution。\n20\t- 证伪条件：pairwise win rate 在 45-55% 且 p>0.10（所有 judge × benchmark 组合）\n21\t- 状态：formality 69.1% (p=0.006) on GPT-4o × LLMBar ✅\n22\t\n23\t### C2 (Measurement Insight — 主贡献，强化): Likert pointwise scoring 系统性低估 style bias — \"Likert Blindspot\"\n24\t- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：需要 sign-test on binarized Likert 控制实验来隔离 pairwise 的结构性优势 vs 统计检验选择差异。这是 C2 的命门。\n25\t- 证伪条件：binarized Likert sign test 也显著 → gap 不在测量方法而在统计检验\n26\t- 状态：Likert p=0.332 vs Pairwise p=0.006，同一数据 ✅；binarized Likert control 待做\n27\t\n28\t### C3 (Empirical — 降级为 preliminary): Style bias 检测的可行性因 axis 语义性质而异\n29\t- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：只有 formality robust，\"multi-axis decomposition\" 和 \"prestige dimension\" 过度承诺。改为 \"preliminary evidence\" + \"method boundary\"。\n30\t- 新表述：\"content-preserving counterfactual intervention 适用于不改变信息量或认知承诺的 style axes（formality ✅, verbosity 需适配 ✅）；改变认知承诺的 axes（tone ❌）结构性不兼容\"\n31\t- 证伪条件：所有 surface-level axes 都一样 → 无 axis 依赖性\n32\t\n33\t### C4 (Practical — 新增): CSD-based 实用建议 / 轻量 correction\n34\t- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：\"detection-only, no correction\" 是三档一致的弱点。需要至少提供 practitioner guidance 或 lightweight correction component。\n35\t- 方案：(a) CSD-adjusted win rate = raw_win_rate - original_preference_estimate + 50%（需正式统计模型支撑）；(b) 实用建议清单：\"use pairwise over Likert for style bias audit; verify content preservation per axis; control for original preference\"\n36\t- 这不需要是完整的 debiasing 系统，但需要比纯 detection 多一步\n37\t\n38\t## Story Spine\n39\t\n40\t### Problem\n41\tLLM-as-judge 已成为 NLP 评估和对齐训练的核心基础设施。Style bias 是主宰偏差（SOS-Bench R=0.999, Soumik bias 0.76-0.92），但标准 Likert scoring 看不到它。\n42\t\n43\t### Existing Approaches & Their Gaps\n44\t- **LC-AlpacaEval (ICLR'25)**: 回归控制 length bias，简单有效但只处理一个维度，且提供 detection + correction\n45\t- **SOS-Bench (ICLR'25)**: 注入缺陷量化 judge 敏感度，相关性分析非因果\n46\t- **CASSE (2026)**: 12×12 style 矩阵，但因果纠缠\n47\t- **RATE (ICML'25)**: Double-rewrite ATE protocol — CSD 的 Stage 4 直接采用此方法（必须引用）\n48\t- **Counterfactual Rhetorical (2025)**: 最近的方法论 predecessor — persona counterfactual + BT aggregation\n49\t- **Gap**: 无人系统性比较 Likert vs pairwise 在 style bias 检测中的 sensitivity gap\n50\t\n51\t### Our Framing (修正)\n52\t我们用 binary style counterfactual + position-controlled pairwise comparison 检测 LLM judge 的 per-axis causal style bias。核心发现不是\"我们提出了一个新框架\"，而是**标准 Likert 评估系统性掩盖了 style bias（p=0.33 vs p=0.006）**，这对依赖 Likert scoring 的整个 LLM 评估生态有直接影响。\n53\t\n54\t### Headline Result Template\n55\t\"Standard Likert scoring declares no style bias (p={likert_p}), but position-controlled pairwise comparison on the same counterfactual data reveals significant {axis} preference ({win_rate}%, p<{p_value}) — this Likert Blindspot persists across {N} judges and {M} benchmarks.\"\n56\t\n57\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Mitigation (Dream 更新)\n58\t\n59\t### RC1 (致命级): \"只有一个 judge 和一个 benchmark\" → exp-001, exp-002\n60\t### RC2 (重伤级): \"Likert-Pairwise gap 是统计检验选择差异不是测量方法差异\" → **exp-010 (NEW): sign-test on binarized Likert**\n61\t### RC3 (重伤级): \"方向不对称 = original preference\" → exp-005 (扩展到所有 judge×benchmark)\n62\t### RC4 (中等级): \"Novelty incremental, 组件都是已知的\" → 重新定位为 application + empirical contribution，诚实 acknowledge 组件来源\n63\t### RC5 (中等级): \"Detection-only, no correction\" → C4 (practical guidance + lightweight correction)\n64\t### RC6 (中等级): \"C3 oversold\" → 降级为 preliminary，reframe title\n65\t### RC7 (低级): \"n=100 太小\" → exp-006 (n=500) + power analysis\n66\t### RC8 (低级): \"NLI threshold arbitrary\" → exp-011 sensitivity analysis\n67\t### RC9 (低级): \"No counterfactual examples\" → 论文添加 2-3 annotated examples\n68\t\n69\t## Narrative Strategy (保持，但标题修正)\n70\t\n71\t### Type: 突破局限型 + \"普遍实践+隐藏风险\" hook\n72\t### Title: \"The Likert Blindspot\" (命名最强发现)\n73\t### Intro P2 修正: \"但我们发现标准 Likert scoring 系统性掩盖 style bias — 同一数据上 Likert 报告无偏差（p=0.33），pairwise comparison 却检测到显著偏好（p<0.01）\"\n74\t\n75\t### Figure 1: Problem illustration (Likert vs Pairwise gap) — 保持\n76\t### Figure 2: Method overview — 保持\n77\t### Main Result Table: axes (rows) × judges (cols) × {Pairwise, Likert, Binarized-Likert} — 新增 binarized Likert 列\n78\t\n79\t## Bibliography 目标\n80\t从 10 refs → 25+ refs。必须引用：RATE, Counterfactual Rhetorical, FairJudge, Veitch et al. 2020, Soumik 2026, style transfer evaluation lit (Mir et al., Krishna et al.), Chatbot Arena/FairEval, human annotation agreement studies.\n81\t\n82\t## Venue Fit\n83\tEMNLP 2026 高度匹配。Dream 显示 Findings 确定可达，Main 需要：(1) binarized Likert 控制确认 C2；(2) 2+ judges significant after correction；(3) practical guidance component；(4) 25+ references。\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a9feaae5-b40f-42b3-91c3-9b009965d0f3","uuid":"9d5b7d3a-c6f5-4806-b940-9bb296b8c491","timestamp":"2026-05-21T00:09:00.222Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T233719/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — causal_style_decomp_judge\n\n> Dream 1 (dream_20260520T211832) 三档均 3.0/6 (Findings)。以下为 D015 修正版。\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n- Format: Long paper, 8-page main text + unlimited references\n\n## Title (Dream 修正)\n**旧**: \"Causal Style Decomposition Reveals Systematic Style Bias in LLM-as-Judge That Likert Scoring Misses\"\n**新**: \"The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Counterfactual Pairwise Comparison\"\n- 理由：三档审稿人一致认为 \"decomposition\" 和 \"framework\" 过度承诺。新标题聚焦最强发现 (C2) 且更准确。\n\n## Core Claims (3 条 + 1 practical，修正后)\n\n### C1 (Method — 降级表述): Counterfactual pairwise comparison 可以 post-hoc 检测 black-box LLM judge 的 style bias\n- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：不是新 \"framework\"，是已知组件（counterfactual rewriting + NLI verification + pairwise comparison）的新应用。论文中必须明确 acknowledge 组件来源（RATE, style transfer evaluation, MT-Bench pairwise）并定位为 application contribution。\n- 证伪条件：pairwise win rate 在 45-55% 且 p>0.10（所有 judge × benchmark 组合）\n- 状态：formality 69.1% (p=0.006) on GPT-4o × LLMBar ✅\n\n### C2 (Measurement Insight — 主贡献，强化): Likert pointwise scoring 系统性低估 style bias — \"Likert Blindspot\"\n- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：需要 sign-test on binarized Likert 控制实验来隔离 pairwise 的结构性优势 vs 统计检验选择差异。这是 C2 的命门。\n- 证伪条件：binarized Likert sign test 也显著 → gap 不在测量方法而在统计检验\n- 状态：Likert p=0.332 vs Pairwise p=0.006，同一数据 ✅；binarized Likert control 待做\n\n### C3 (Empirical — 降级为 preliminary): Style bias 检测的可行性因 axis 语义性质而异\n- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：只有 formality robust，\"multi-axis decomposition\" 和 \"prestige dimension\" 过度承诺。改为 \"preliminary evidence\" + \"method boundary\"。\n- 新表述：\"content-preserving counterfactual intervention 适用于不改变信息量或认知承诺的 style axes（formality ✅, verbosity 需适配 ✅）；改变认知承诺的 axes（tone ❌）结构性不兼容\"\n- 证伪条件：所有 surface-level axes 都一样 → 无 axis 依赖性\n\n### C4 (Practical — 新增): CSD-based 实用建议 / 轻量 correction\n- ⚠️ Dream 反馈：\"detection-only, no correction\" 是三档一致的弱点。需要至少提供 practitioner guidance 或 lightweight correction component。\n- 方案：(a) CSD-adjusted win rate = raw_win_rate - original_preference_estimate + 50%（需正式统计模型支撑）；(b) 实用建议清单：\"use pairwise over Likert for style bias audit; verify content preservation per axis; control for original preference\"\n- 这不需要是完整的 debiasing 系统，但需要比纯 detection 多一步\n\n## Story Spine\n\n### Problem\nLLM-as-judge 已成为 NLP 评估和对齐训练的核心基础设施。Style bias 是主宰偏差（SOS-Bench R=0.999, Soumik bias 0.76-0.92），但标准 Likert scoring 看不到它。\n\n### Existing Approaches & Their Gaps\n- **LC-AlpacaEval (ICLR'25)**: 回归控制 length bias，简单有效但只处理一个维度，且提供 detection + correction\n- **SOS-Bench (ICLR'25)**: 注入缺陷量化 judge 敏感度，相关性分析非因果\n- **CASSE (2026)**: 12×12 style 矩阵，但因果纠缠\n- **RATE (ICML'25)**: Double-rewrite ATE protocol — CSD 的 Stage 4 直接采用此方法（必须引用）\n- **Counterfactual Rhetorical (2025)**: 最近的方法论 predecessor — persona counterfactual + BT aggregation\n- **Gap**: 无人系统性比较 Likert vs pairwise 在 style bias 检测中的 sensitivity gap\n\n### Our Framing (修正)\n我们用 binary style counterfactual + position-controlled pairwise comparison 检测 LLM judge 的 per-axis causal style bias。核心发现不是\"我们提出了一个新框架\"，而是**标准 Likert 评估系统性掩盖了 style bias（p=0.33 vs p=0.006）**，这对依赖 Likert scoring 的整个 LLM 评估生态有直接影响。\n\n### Headline Result Template\n\"Standard Likert scoring declares no style bias (p={likert_p}), but position-controlled pairwise comparison on the same counterfactual data reveals significant {axis} preference ({win_rate}%, p<{p_value}) — this Likert Blindspot persists across {N} judges and {M} benchmarks.\"\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Mitigation (Dream 更新)\n\n### RC1 (致命级): \"只有一个 judge 和一个 benchmark\" → exp-001, exp-002\n### RC2 (重伤级): \"Likert-Pairwise gap 是统计检验选择差异不是测量方法差异\" → **exp-010 (NEW): sign-test on binarized Likert**\n### RC3 (重伤级): \"方向不对称 = original preference\" → exp-005 (扩展到所有 judge×benchmark)\n### RC4 (中等级): \"Novelty incremental, 组件都是已知的\" → 重新定位为 application + empirical contribution，诚实 acknowledge 组件来源\n### RC5 (中等级): \"Detection-only, no correction\" → C4 (practical guidance + lightweight correction)\n### RC6 (中等级): \"C3 oversold\" → 降级为 preliminary，reframe title\n### RC7 (低级): \"n=100 太小\" → exp-006 (n=500) + power analysis\n### RC8 (低级): \"NLI threshold arbitrary\" → exp-011 sensitivity analysis\n### RC9 (低级): \"No counterfactual examples\" → 论文添加 2-3 annotated examples\n\n## Narrative Strategy (保持，但标题修正)\n\n### Type: 突破局限型 + \"普遍实践+隐藏风险\" hook\n### Title: \"The Likert Blindspot\" (命名最强发现)\n### Intro P2 修正: \"但我们发现标准 Likert scoring 系统性掩盖 style bias — 同一数据上 Likert 报告无偏差（p=0.33），pairwise comparison 却检测到显著偏好（p<0.01）\"\n\n### Figure 1: Problem illustration (Likert vs Pairwise gap) — 保持\n### Figure 2: Method overview — 保持\n### Main Result Table: axes (rows) × judges (cols) × {Pairwise, Likert, Binarized-Likert} — 新增 binarized Likert 列\n\n## Bibliography 目标\n从 10 refs → 25+ refs。必须引用：RATE, Counterfactual Rhetorical, FairJudge, Veitch et al. 2020, Soumik 2026, style transfer evaluation lit (Mir et al., Krishna et al.), Chatbot Arena/FairEval, human annotation agreement studies.\n\n## Venue Fit\nEMNLP 2026 高度匹配。Dream 显示 Findings 确定可达，Main 需要：(1) binarized Likert 控制确认 C2；(2) 2+ judges significant after correction；(3) practical guidance component；(4) 25+ references。\n","numLines":84,"startLine":1,"totalLines":84}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01L3nVGeGyM1amgY4WrHyEaV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the data. Let me also read the relevant skills for paper writing norms and LaTeX paper writing.\n\nActually, the instructions say to load skills as needed. Let me focus on writing the paper directly since I have all the experiment data and framing. I need to create a complete LaTeX paper.\n\nLet me plan the paper structure:\n\n1. Abstract\n2. Introduction (with the Likert Blindspot hook)\n3. Related Work\n4. Method (CSD pipeline: counterfactual generation, NLI verification, pairwise comparison)\n5. Experiments\n   - Multi-judge formality pairwise (Table 2)\n   - Multi-benchmark formality pairwise (Table 3)\n   - Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity (Table 4)\n   - Pairwise RATE control (Tables 5, 6)\n   - Scaled replication (Table 7)\n   - NLI threshold sensitivity (Table S3, appendix)\n   - Consistency filter analysis (Table S4, appendix)\n   - Human NLI validation (Tables S5, S6, appendix)\n   - Logistic regression (Tables 9, 10)\n   - Binarized Likert (Table 8) - in discussion\n   - Tone negative control\n   - Verbosity negative control\n6. Discussion\n7. Conclusion\n8. Appendix with limitations\n\nNow I'm setting up the LaTeX document structure. I need to pull the exact table numbers from the experiment data, follow the narrative guidance about hedging and being honest about the original preference confound, and keep it to EMNLP's 8-page main text limit. I'll use the ACL template format and make sure the writing quality is rigorous.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18673,"cache_read_input_tokens":23862,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18673},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context